{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy","id":1093829,"title":"Is VV Going to be Too Edgy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-17T14:46:32-07:00","id":1093829,"title":"Is VV Going to be Too Edgy?","content":"Hey guys. So i've seen that criticism about this new edition of VTM. That they are trying too hard to be dark or edgy. And i'm lost because i don't know where is that coming from. I agree wholeheartedly with other criticism like they talking smack about nwod and how they hired insane criminal Zak Smith. But after many speeches about how they want to deal with real world conflicts and how they are mature. i've having trouble understanding where all that supposed edginess is coming from. Is it because of Martin Ericcson himself? I Know he's flamboyant and talks funny and etc... But he insists he's doing something mature and serious here. So why do you guys think new white wolf is gonna be all katanas and trenchcoats not serious stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T15:04:15-07:00","id":1093843,"title":"","content":"First, we should establish what &quot;edgy&quot; actually means, and that it is a good thing or bad, because I suspect it's differing a lot between individuals here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/edgy\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/entries/icons/original/000/014/745/139035361828.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/edgy\" target=\"_blank\"> Edgy | Know Your Meme </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/edgy\" target=\"_blank\"> http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/edgy </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> &ldquo;Edgy&rdquo; is an English slang term used to describe things, behaviors or trends which are provocative or avant-garde, and is often used to describe things tha </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/edgy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/edgy</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/edgy\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn.dictionary.com/logo-vocab-com-CKu1F3aD.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/edgy\" target=\"_blank\"> EDGY Definition &amp; Meaning | Dictionary.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/edgy\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.dictionary.com/browse/edgy </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> EDGY definition: nervously irritable; impatient and anxious. See examples of edgy used in a sentence. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, to me, being edgy isn't a slur, but it could be pretentious, if taking too far. Of course, what considers &quot;taking too far&quot; is highly personal. To be honest, for a <i>lot</i> of people, playing vampires struggling for their dwindling humanity is <i>already</i> pretentious and edgy.<br /> <br /> For example, that they want to incorporate real-world phenomena (I suspect that's the main reason why people are crying &quot;edgy&quot;) and &quot;recent ones&quot; too is too much for some people, but to me it isn't edgy in a bad way.<br /> <br /> Also, WoD was always edgy. It was &quot;dark&quot;, it was &quot;gothic&quot;, it was &quot;punk&quot;, it was big into counterculture. It is already edgy and I love it for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-17-2017, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T15:11:16-07:00","id":1093852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093843#post1093843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, we should establish what &quot;edgy&quot; actually means, and that it is a good thing or bad, because I suspect it's differing a lot between individuals here.</div> </div> </div> </div>When people say White Wolf is trying to be edgy, they often mean they trying to be shocking just for the sake of being shocking,Having gory imagery just for the sake of gorey imagery,having lots of swearing blood sex and gratuitious violence just for the sake of it. I've seen so many people worried about that and i don't know the basis of their concernsss","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T15:22:47-07:00","id":1093859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093852#post1093852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When people say White Wolf is trying to be edgy, they often mean they trying to be shocking just for the sake of being shocking,Having gory imagery just for the sake of gorey imagery,having lots of swearing blood sex and gratuitious violence just for the sake of it. I've seen so many people worried about that and i don't know the basis of their concernsss</div> </div> </div> </div>Being shocking for just shock value, I suspect the biggest reason is the aforementioned plan for using recent events and how Martin talked about it and about using other controversial topics in the game. Some people didn't like that, for personal reasons, although I have no problems with it, I actually liked what he said about all of that.<br /> <br /> Also, some things, like hiring ZakS, the language and story of the VtM Prelude game and Martin's novella in the fiction anthology they (re)published lately. Those could be a worrying sign of them taking the route of &quot;controversy, blood, gore and sex&quot; just to be shocking. I could understand those concerns, although other things they did, like the LARPS and events organized are fairly encouraging and they met a wide approval, as far as I got it, so I reserve judgment for the final product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-17-2017, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T15:28:08-07:00","id":1093864,"title":"","content":"I personally don't care who works on it, it's going to be a lot of people and I separate art from the artist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T15:57:53-07:00","id":1093877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093864#post1093864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally don't care who works on it, it's going to be a lot of people and I separate art from the artist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that's why I generally don't dig too deep into who are the artists IRL and who made what? I want to enjoy nice things and sometimes awful people are making nice things. Also, I don't want my involvement with persons to color my evaluation of a product.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, it'll be a collaborative endeavor. Even if I'd have hate Martin for whatever reasons, I wouldn't write off V5 for just that.<br /> <br /> Just for the record, I don't think anyone in the WW team is an awful person. I don't know any of them personally and yes, Martin could be pretty theatrical, but some of the creative types aer like that. Overall, I don't have a bad impression about them, based on their talks and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-17-2017, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T15:58:42-07:00","id":1093878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093859#post1093859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being shocking for just shock value, I suspect the biggest reason is the aforementioned plan for using recent events and how Martin talked about it and about using other controversial topics in the game. Some people didn't like that, for personal reasons, although I have no problems with it, I actually liked what he said about all of that.<br /> <br /> Also, some things, like hiring ZakS, the language and story of the VtM Prelude game and Martin's novella in the fiction anthology they (re)published lately. Those could be a worrying sign of them taking the route of &quot;controversy, blood, gore and sex&quot; just to be shocking. I could understand those concerns, although other things they did, like the LARPS and events organized are fairly encouraging and they met a wide approval, as far as I got it, so I reserve judgment for the final product.</div> </div> </div> </div>i too am reserving judgement for when the book comes. i don't anything about the preluides though,could it be they were too shocking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T16:08:31-07:00","id":1093881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093878#post1093878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i don't anything about the preluides though,could it be they were too shocking?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more like it pushed personal buttons in some people <i>on top of</i> (and in conjunction with) the whole ZakS debacle. I think they wouldn't do it the same way a second time.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, End of the Line, Convention of Thorns and now Enlightement in Blood was cherished and those were big &quot;products&quot;, actually made/organized by them and I didn't heard from anyone that they were shocking just for shock value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T17:35:14-07:00","id":1093916,"title":"","content":"I expect the Vamprie flamewars to make the mage 2e to revised Flamewars look tame. Like the differences between Napoleonic warfare and ww2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T19:01:41-07:00","id":1093943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093916#post1093916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect the Vamprie flamewars to make the mage 2e to revised Flamewars look tame. Like the differences between Napoleonic warfare and ww2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fandom a can be quite aggressive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T20:31:05-07:00","id":1093966,"title":"","content":"Strangely enough, I find the VtM forum to be fairly polite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T20:40:13-07:00","id":1093969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093966#post1093966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strangely enough, I find the VtM forum to be fairly polite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the mods here do a pretty good job of keeping conversations civil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T20:43:02-07:00","id":1093970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093966#post1093966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strangely enough, I find the VtM forum to be fairly polite.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is, everyone who ought to be outraged already did and their outrage-o-meter just being depleted. It might refill later, but now I sense more ignoring and disinterest.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093969#post1093969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the mods here do a pretty good job of keeping conversations civil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that one too. Kudos to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T21:30:08-07:00","id":1093983,"title":"","content":"As part of the &quot;3edgy5me&quot; crowd, the issue is not one of degree, but of reason (or rather, the lack thereof). I've said before and I'll say again, I have no problem with &quot;edginess&quot; <i>per se</i>, I only take issue with it being for edginess' sake. Shock is perfectly fine when it's used for a purpose, but it's obnoxious when it's only used to be shocking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093878#post1093878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i too am reserving judgement for when the book comes. i don't anything about the preluides though,could it be they were too shocking?</div> </div> </div> </div>The two big issues most folks have taken with the preludes are A.) that they were co-written by Zak S, who has a history of stalking and harassing a lot of people including David Hill, and B.) the depiction of one of the characters, a trans woman who claims she feeds by calling uber, and if her driver is male, telling them she is trans and has not surgically transitioned (specifically saying &quot;so I'm trans and I have, like, a cock&quot;), offering him a handjob (which she claims they <i>never</i> refuse) and then kills and eats him after if she didn't like his reaction to her revelation. Oh, and she also happens to share the first name of a trans writer who Zak has clashed with in the past.<br /> <br /> The issue here is not that the preludes are <i>too</i> edgy, it's that they are <i>tastelessly</i> and <i>pointlessly</i> edgy. And that pretty much seems to be exactly what Martin and co are going for. They gladly hired Zak despite being fully aware of the controversy surrounding him (possibly even <i>due to it</i>?) and tried to gaslight the fan community with a blog post on their website claiming that they were aware of the accusations against Zak and that there was no evidence to substantiate them. And in response to the criticism of the atrociously portrayed trans character, they basically just said &quot;we think she's awesome.&quot; Which is pretty fucking gross, honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T21:50:24-07:00","id":1093986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093966#post1093966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strangely enough, I find the VtM forum to be fairly polite.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> VV hasn't been released yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T21:52:03-07:00","id":1093987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093986#post1093986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> VV hasn't been released yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine white wolf will have their own forums up and running by then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T22:13:33-07:00","id":1093990,"title":"","content":"G-d: &quot;What's the matter, Az?&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;I have come to believe in you, because I now feel abandoned by you.&quot;<br /> G-d: &quot;Sticking to previous editions, then?&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;You know the answer to that.&quot;<br /> G-d: &quot;Jack smiles upon you, even if I don't.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T22:28:26-07:00","id":1093994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093987#post1093987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine white wolf will have their own forums up and running by then.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I expect they will need serious moderation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T22:34:18-07:00","id":1093997,"title":"","content":"That is what I did with 4e Shadowrun after I played some 5e Shadowrun games. If 5e WoD ends up being horrific, the old fans will probably stay with the editions that they prefer (or, more likely, the heavily modified editions that they make perfect for them with their dozens of house rules), and Paradox will likely sell off the IP to another interested party because there will not be enough interest to make their investment worthwhile. Perhaps Disney would be interested in adding it to their IP collection along with Marvel and Star Wars (given the quality of the Marvel Cinematic Universe, I am not sure that Disney buying the IP would actually be a bad thing). Until it comes out though, we should probably keep calm and reserve judgment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T22:34:56-07:00","id":1093998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093994#post1093994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And I expect they will need serious moderation</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, just lay the ground rule of no edition Waring and after the first couple of bans people will take it somewhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T23:08:23-07:00","id":1094003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093997#post1093997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is what I did with 4e Shadowrun after I played some 5e Shadowrun games. If 5e WoD ends up being horrific, the old fans will probably stay with the editions that they prefer (or, more likely, the heavily modified editions that they make perfect for them with their dozens of house rules), and Paradox will likely sell off the IP to another interested party because there will not be enough interest to make their investment worthwhile. Perhaps Disney would be interested in adding it to their IP collection along with Marvel and Star Wars (given the quality of the Marvel Cinematic Universe, I am not sure that Disney buying the IP would actually be a bad thing). Until it comes out though, we should probably keep calm and reserve judgment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I am calm. I know LARPers who thought BNS changes were too extreme. While all a very interesting take it basically makes you have to start over with the new stuff. Mechanically, Metaplotwise etc and that's before Sabbat being relegated to some far off suppliment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T23:51:43-07:00","id":1094012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy#post1093829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... they hired insane criminal Zak Smith...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Not OK, still counts as a personal attack regardless of people's feelings about the guy. I'm letting you off with a warning, please don't do this again.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T00:07:37-07:00","id":1094017,"title":"","content":"I've just finished playing We eat blood and now I'm starting Mage refuge. While I was sceptical at first with Vampire game the 2 last chapters were very interesting and I even liked one character (Anis which is weird for me) and dialogue between Case and main antagonist is epic, i felt that the game without some controversial things would be better. I felt that it was forced in the game to shock and I wasn't shocked at all but unnecessary distasted. I think that they have to balance between normal and edgy ideas cause exaggerating it would be ridiculous. Thats why we eat blood was quite funny, but it wasn't very good.<br /> I've started mage refuge and after first chapter i think it might be better, at first glance more interesting, but I have my personal opinion about main theme of this story and because of Darksider watching I'll keep it for myself. Balance is the key word - game should be thrilling, sometimes edgy but not ridiculous. Not at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T00:12:41-07:00","id":1094019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093983#post1093983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They gladly hired Zak despite being fully aware of the controversy surrounding him (possibly even <i>due to it</i>?)...</div> </div> </div> </div>While not the only reason people are worried, this is a great example.<br /> <br /> On their blog, they said they welcomed &quot;some&quot; of the controversy they knew Zak would bring with him. Now, what they fairly clearly wanted, was the ire of misogynists, transphobes, and so on that Zak and Sarah would (and did) evoke by putting a trans character so front and center in the Prelude. But they did not think through how the execution of this would play with both the RPG community vis a vis Zak's history there, and the trans community that might not exactly like being used to troll bigots to make WWP look progressive. Sarah's reaction to the fall out from the preview was particularly telling; neither WWP or Zak prepped her in the slightest for the predictable backlash she was in for.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, while we don't have V5, so we don't know where it will end up, Martin and WWP keep promising things that feel either incompatible or exceedingly difficult to balance. What little evidence we have (one short story, two Prelude interactive fictions) consistently shows WWP failing to meet the expectations they're setting; and each time in the direction of being &quot;too much edge for the sake of edge&quot; than any other option. The LARP events seem to be doing better walking that line, but a lot more people are involved in making those happen than have control over the creative content in V5 (at the moment, we only know of three people actively writing V5: Martin, Karim, and Ken). If we also take in more than just the recent WWP involved LARPs... well Martin's history gets a bit more muddy.<br /> <br /> Is V5 oing to be too edgy? Who knows?<br /> <br /> But the combination of uncertainty, a lot of bad PR, and a lot of cherry picking of which parts of the community they actively engage in, means a lot of fans feel burnt on giving WWP the benefit of the doubt.<br /> <br /> The cherry picking is probably one of the worst things in all this. WWP hasn't ventured to any of the major RPG forums. They haven't even come here. They haven't engaged with plenty of the bigger LARP organizations besides chatting with their leaders at the Grand Masquerade. So they're taking zero control over the narrative here; which is very disappointing because the groups that are getting the most attention seem far more mollified about their concerns. Meanwhile those of us that have been playing the WoD in TT, or PbP, or chats, or whatever get told that WWP doesn't actually consider that contribution to the viability of the WoD IP important. LARP is getting the most support, and the most engagement, because they're the true torchbearers that have kept the WoD alive according to Shane (you know... one of the two LARP people WWP has pulled in from BNS).<br /> <br /> So my goodwill is gone. Until WWP proves to me that they learned why the anthology reissue, and the Zak debacle, and the meh-ness of the Preludes main content, were all problems, I'm going to believe we'll see more severed anuses (wish that was a joke...) than games that walk the line of edgy and well handled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T02:27:51-07:00","id":1094051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094019#post1094019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> But they did not think through how the execution of this would play with both the RPG community vis a vis Zak's history there, and the trans community that might not exactly like being used to troll bigots to make WWP look progressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mom bought me Werewolf the Apocalypse at the age of 14 because I've been begging her to do so. I was amazed by Albrecht character in the comics - fallen garou hero - that was the main reason. Question is - would I buy WtA for my son/daughter if the main character would be a girl with d..k? No way. And I don't agree that WtA or Vampire is so mature. They want to make mature game, but in my opinion transsexual theme is no mature at all. It's just is. I understand that my wishlist for WoD and how it should look in my imagination doesn't matter at all. But my money matters. And every fan money matters. If they would keep their money in the wallet it would lead to two conclusions : WWP would have to try harder and make game majority of players want or sell the game. I truly have hope that after negative feedback they will stop to think for a while. My hope is that they already stoped to think, by hiring Hite for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T03:00:47-07:00","id":1094054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093983#post1093983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As part of the &amp;quot;3edgy5me&amp;quot; crowd, the issue is not one of degree, but of reason (or rather, the lack thereof). I've said before and I'll say again, I have no problem with &amp;quot;edginess&amp;quot; <i>per se</i>, I only take issue with it being for edginess' sake. Shock is perfectly fine when it's used for a purpose, but it's obnoxious when it's only used to be shocking.<br /> <br /> <br /> The two big issues most folks have taken with the preludes are A.) that they were co-written by Zak S, who has a history of stalking and harassing a lot of people including David Hill, and B.) the depiction of one of the characters, a trans woman who claims she feeds by calling uber, and if her driver is male, telling them she is trans and has not surgically transitioned (specifically saying &amp;quot;so I'm trans and I have, like, a cock&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, offering him a handjob (which she claims they <i>never</i> refuse) and then kills and eats him after if she didn't like his reaction to her revelation. Oh, and she also happens to share the first name of a trans writer who Zak has clashed with in the past.<br /> <br /> The issue here is not that the preludes are <i>too</i> edgy, it's that they are <i>tastelessly</i> and <i>pointlessly</i> edgy. And that pretty much seems to be exactly what Martin and co are going for. They gladly hired Zak despite being fully aware of the controversy surrounding him (possibly even <i>due to it</i>?) and tried to gaslight the fan community with a blog post on their website claiming that they were aware of the accusations against Zak and that there was no evidence to substantiate them. And in response to the criticism of the atrociously portrayed trans character, they basically just said &amp;quot;we think she's awesome.&amp;quot; Which is pretty fucking gross, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>A trans character got the shaft? I hate when that happens. So you definitely have a point. A prelude like that is sure to turn people of","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T03:04:46-07:00","id":1094055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094019#post1094019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While not the only reason people are worried, this is a great example.<br /> <br /> On their blog, they said they welcomed &amp;quot;some&amp;quot; of the controversy they knew Zak would bring with him. Now, what they fairly clearly wanted, was the ire of misogynists, transphobes, and so on that Zak and Sarah would (and did) evoke by putting a trans character so front and center in the Prelude. But they did not think through how the execution of this would play with both the RPG community vis a vis Zak's history there, and the trans community that might not exactly like being used to troll bigots to make WWP look progressive. Sarah's reaction to the fall out from the preview was particularly telling; neither WWP or Zak prepped her in the slightest for the predictable backlash she was in for.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, while we don't have V5, so we don't know where it will end up, Martin and WWP keep promising things that feel either incompatible or exceedingly difficult to balance. What little evidence we have (one short story, two Prelude interactive fictions) consistently shows WWP failing to meet the expectations they're setting; and each time in the direction of being &amp;quot;too much edge for the sake of edge&amp;quot; than any other option. The LARP events seem to be doing better walking that line, but a lot more people are involved in making those happen than have control over the creative content in V5 (at the moment, we only know of three people actively writing V5: Martin, Karim, and Ken). If we also take in more than just the recent WWP involved LARPs... well Martin's history gets a bit more muddy.<br /> <br /> Is V5 oing to be too edgy? Who knows?<br /> <br /> But the combination of uncertainty, a lot of bad PR, and a lot of cherry picking of which parts of the community they actively engage in, means a lot of fans feel burnt on giving WWP the benefit of the doubt.<br /> <br /> The cherry picking is probably one of the worst things in all this. WWP hasn't ventured to any of the major RPG forums. They haven't even come here. They haven't engaged with plenty of the bigger LARP organizations besides chatting with their leaders at the Grand Masquerade. So they're taking zero control over the narrative here; which is very disappointing because the groups that are getting the most attention seem far more mollified about their concerns. Meanwhile those of us that have been playing the WoD in TT, or PbP, or chats, or whatever get told that WWP doesn't actually consider that contribution to the viability of the WoD IP important. LARP is getting the most support, and the most engagement, because they're the true torchbearers that have kept the WoD alive according to Shane (you know... one of the two LARP people WWP has pulled in from BNS).<br /> <br /> So my goodwill is gone. Until WWP proves to me that they learned why the anthology reissue, and the Zak debacle, and the meh-ness of the Preludes main content, were all problems, I'm going to believe we'll see more severed anuses (wish that was a joke...) than games that walk the line of edgy and well handled.</div> </div> </div> </div>But wanst Gore a important part of the aesthetic since the beginning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T03:28:30-07:00","id":1094056,"title":"","content":"What I see is that WWP as a Swedish company has a progressive/liberal culture that maybe can shock more conservative people from other cultures. I mean, is it ok to rip people while in Crinos but is not ok a trans character? I admit that the depiction of the prelude character is weird, but I have created even weirder NPC in my chronicle.<br /> <br /> It seems that wanting to speak about more 'real' stuff is annoying people, I read a review about the Mage Prelude saying that if they wanted to know about the refugee crisis they would have watched a documentary about that. It looks very narrow minded and that all the game is about is ripping enemies apart as some sort of superheroes-that-drink-blood or d&amp;d.<br /> <br /> I think that 25 years ago Vampire: the Masquerade was edgy and now they try to do this again. It's good that they not only update the mechanics but also they update the flavor, far from the powergaming game that become the 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1750-dasyrch","name":"dasyrch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T04:00:32-07:00","id":1094063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dasyrch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094056#post1094056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I see is that WWP as a Swedish company has a progressive/liberal culture that maybe can shock more conservative people from other cultures. I mean, is it ok to rip people while in Crinos but is not ok a trans character? I admit that the depiction of the prelude character is weird, but I have created even weirder NPC in my chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are liberal?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Try to but beer at normal european cost in Scandinavian countries. Good luck. What about no go zones/cities, where police patrols doesn''t appear? Is Sweeden Different? Yes. Opened for refugees? Yes. More tolerate? Yes! But are transsexuals, weird characters shocking? edgy? mature style for open minded people? I'm rather conservative person but it doesn't shock me. It just is. they are forcing the theme because majority of european countries are political correct and it is popular to be gay/trans/other.maby weird, so their societies accept for example transsexuals. Would it be shocking to them if they already see it day by day on street of their cities? Would the game pumped in those themes be interesting? What about good story? Good plot, storyline, characters with depth ( I agree that trans could be good character , but it has to have a fu..ng good background), mythology. Where's the spark that created WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dasyrch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094056#post1094056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It seems that wanting to speak about more 'real' stuff is annoying people, I read a review about the Mage Prelude saying that if they wanted to know about the refugee crisis they would have watched a documentary about that. It looks very narrow minded and that all the game is about is ripping enemies apart as some sort of superheroes-that-drink-blood or d&amp;d.</div> </div> </div> </div>More real? Let's talk about cheating in country goverments elections, WW3 in the cyberspace, rise of China, human trade, corruption, terrorism, religion wars (I agree we're in second middle ages), conspiracies. I think that in Werewolf Larp storyline changes are awesome. Truly I think that. And there are no trans/refugees? That's why I loved WoD trailer - i think it's war with humanity, shadow war. And that's good.<br /> <br /> No offence<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And by the way. In my point of view here are examples of the mature theme in WoD.<br /> <br /> 1. Mythology of the red talons in tribebook revised. After reading it I stopped to think about it and conclusions were rather dark.<br /> <br /> 2. Book of the Weaver - tools of the Weaver, tools of cosmic entity that gave human like dogma., Humanity as a weaver tribe. Concept of Machine. It was scary for me. Because being only a ratchet in the well oiled machine, well controlled machine which is humanity, living in hell of peoples constant race for fame/cash/position - it is so real. And I'm afraid that words from Book of weaver became reality. That's in my opinion is mature and truly scary.<br /> <br /> 3. Description of something like Wyrm place in the Rage Acropss the heavens. lifless, cold, dead. No stars, no light. It made a huge imprerssion on me. Impression I don't want to repeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 05-18-2017, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T05:21:56-07:00","id":1094088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094051#post1094051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question is - would I buy WtA for my son/daughter if the main character would be a girl with d..k? No way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's your decision as a parent I guess, but not at all the point I was trying to make. As a girl with a dick myself, I'm all for trans representation. It's just that the character was negative representation.<br /> <br /> Announcing that you are trans to random uber drivers is incredibly dangerous for real trans people, and while probably less dangerous for her as a vampire, still seems out of character for a trans character. The fact that she offers the driver sexual favors and then murders the driver if she didn't like his answers to her social justice questions presents her as both incredibly promiscuous and sexually predatory, both of which are negative stereotypes about trans women, not to mention playing into the stereotype of &quot;SJWs&quot; being violently committed to their views. The fact that she claims her victims never refuse the offer of sexual favors is unrealistic, and suggests that either she is lying to make herself seem more sexually appealing than she is, or that she is using her vampire powers to take advantage of the men she is preying on. Neither option is positive trans representation, and the latter further doubles down on the stereotype of trans women as sexual predators.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094051#post1094051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't agree that WtA or Vampire is so mature. They want to make mature game, but in my opinion transsexual theme is no mature at all. It's just is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having transgender (the preferred term over transsexual) characters isn't a theme. Trans people exist in real life and should accordingly be represented in fiction. However, as a marginalized and oppressed group, representation needs to be handled responsibly. That is to say, in a way that does not ridicule the character(s) on the basis of their transness or reinforce harmful stereotypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T05:27:43-07:00","id":1094089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dasyrch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094056#post1094056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it ok to rip people while in Crinos but is not ok a trans character? I admit that the depiction of the prelude character is weird, but I have created even weirder NPC in my chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is not the inclusion of a trans character (trans representation is a good thing), or that her depiction was &quot;weird.&quot; The issue is that her depiction reinforces harmful stereotypes of trans women, and that their response to criticism of the character was to dismiss it on the basis of her being &quot;a badass.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T05:29:13-07:00","id":1094090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094055#post1094055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But wanst Gore a important part of the aesthetic since the beginning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read Heavy Arms' post at all? A gory aesthetic has next to nothing to do with the point he was making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T05:44:42-07:00","id":1094093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094088#post1094088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's your decision as a parent I guess,.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll become a father this year. After a years of observation I'll have to be extra watchful to protect my child from world sickness. To be clear I'm not speaking about You or transgender persons cause they like everyone they could have good heart and be just a good people. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094088#post1094088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> . The fact that she claims her victims never refuse the offer of sexual favors is unrealistic, and suggests that either she is lying to make herself seem more sexually appealing than she is, or that she is using her vampire powers to take advantage of the men she is preying on. Neither option is positive trans representation, and the latter further doubles down on the stereotype of trans women as sexual predators.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I was rather suprised about reasons she would kill. Besides I preffered help from her than from Morgan. I'm looking for a good storyline in World of Darkness. Not edge over plot. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094088#post1094088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, as a marginalized and oppressed group, representation needs to be handled responsibly .</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowdays I feel that beeing christian means to belong to marginalized and oppressed group. And I live in catholic country. Don't want to know how it looks in western Europe, but from my firneds told me. Bad. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T05:58:51-07:00","id":1094096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094019#post1094019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While not the only reason people are worried, this is a great example.<br /> <br /> On their blog, they said they welcomed &amp;quot;some&amp;quot; of the controversy they knew Zak would bring with him. Now, what they fairly clearly wanted, was the ire of misogynists, transphobes, and so on that Zak and Sarah would (and did) evoke by putting a trans character so front and center in the Prelude. But they did not think through how the execution of this would play with both the RPG community vis a vis Zak's history there, and the trans community that might not exactly like being used to troll bigots to make WWP look progressive. Sarah's reaction to the fall out from the preview was particularly telling; neither WWP or Zak prepped her in the slightest for the predictable backlash she was in for.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, while we don't have V5, so we don't know where it will end up, Martin and WWP keep promising things that feel either incompatible or exceedingly difficult to balance. What little evidence we have (one short story, two Prelude interactive fictions) consistently shows WWP failing to meet the expectations they're setting; and each time in the direction of being &amp;quot;too much edge for the sake of edge&amp;quot; than any other option. The LARP events seem to be doing better walking that line, but a lot more people are involved in making those happen than have control over the creative content in V5 (at the moment, we only know of three people actively writing V5: Martin, Karim, and Ken). If we also take in more than just the recent WWP involved LARPs... well Martin's history gets a bit more muddy.<br /> <br /> Is V5 oing to be too edgy? Who knows?<br /> <br /> But the combination of uncertainty, a lot of bad PR, and a lot of cherry picking of which parts of the community they actively engage in, means a lot of fans feel burnt on giving WWP the benefit of the doubt.<br /> <br /> The cherry picking is probably one of the worst things in all this. WWP hasn't ventured to any of the major RPG forums. They haven't even come here. They haven't engaged with plenty of the bigger LARP organizations besides chatting with their leaders at the Grand Masquerade. So they're taking zero control over the narrative here; which is very disappointing because the groups that are getting the most attention seem far more mollified about their concerns. Meanwhile those of us that have been playing the WoD in TT, or PbP, or chats, or whatever get told that WWP doesn't actually consider that contribution to the viability of the WoD IP important. LARP is getting the most support, and the most engagement, because they're the true torchbearers that have kept the WoD alive according to Shane (you know... one of the two LARP people WWP has pulled in from BNS).<br /> <br /> So my goodwill is gone. Until WWP proves to me that they learned why the anthology reissue, and the Zak debacle, and the meh-ness of the Preludes main content, were all problems, I'm going to believe we'll see more severed anuses (wish that was a joke...) than games that walk the line of edgy and well handled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if I missed the point on my last reply. Are you saying people would more accepting of new white wolf if they reached out more to people and explain their plans better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T06:07:59-07:00","id":1094097,"title":"","content":"Lots of hot takes.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, the Werewolf the Apocalypse video game and V5 will be home runs and a blast to play which in the end, is all that really matters to myself(and Paradox).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T06:15:36-07:00","id":1094099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094097#post1094097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of hot takes.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, the Werewolf the Apocalypse video game and V5 will be home runs and a blast to play which in the end, is all that really matters to myself(and Paradox).</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf the Apocalypse video game is the one I'm waiting for. Are You optimistic about Cyanide? I mendtioned it before somewhere - Focus home interactive made in my opinion good games or participated in their creation. Cyanide not exactly. I know, Styx and Blood bowl, are good. I'm looking for Call of Cthulhu because it looks very good at trailers, still waiting for gameplay. But are you optimistic about WtA in Cyanide hands? Look at Confrontation, Game of thrones, even Deathwing wasn't the best.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T06:53:07-07:00","id":1094108,"title":"","content":"I would have rather that they licensed it to a larger video game company. Cyanide has 70 employees, which means that they will contract out most of their art design, programming, testing, etc to other companies. That creates inconsistent quality and delays. A properly done WtA video game will cost around $40 million to make. I will be very disappointed with we get a Minecraft version of WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T07:28:54-07:00","id":1094118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094051#post1094051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question is - would I buy WtA for my son/daughter if the main character would be a girl with d..k? No way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That you describe trans people as &quot;girls with dicks&quot;? Not okay. I'm hoping this is just a language and cultural issue. Please tell me it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T07:46:33-07:00","id":1094124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094097#post1094097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of hot takes.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, the Werewolf the Apocalypse video game and V5 will be home runs and a blast to play which in the end, is all that really matters to myself(and Paradox).</div> </div> </div> </div>The video games will be the real money Akers yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T07:52:46-07:00","id":1094125,"title":"","content":"It is also biologically incorrect. That would be more of an insult for intersex people who identify as female. A transwoman would be better described as transitioning or transitioned from men (male gender) to women (female gender), whether or not they have gone through sexual reassignment surgery. If they have experienced sexual reassignment, they no longer have male genitalia, so the insult would be inaccurate.<br /> <br /> My problem with the representation of the trans person is that it made her sound like a sex-crazed serial killer, which is a stereotypical conservative representation of trans people from the 1990s. A more poignant and less stereotypical representation would have been a trans women who was Embraced before sexual reassignment and has to deal with a male sexed body that rejects the hormones she was taking to feminize her body and that heals any modification to her body, no matter how extreme. <br /> <br /> The horror would be the body horror of being eternally trapped in the wrong body, in a conservative undead society that rejects the claims that you are a woman, without any recourse except for insanity or suicide. Such a person would be tempted to join the Sabbat so she could benefit from Vicissitude in order to have the female body that she desires, but that may be just another form of insanity or suicide. That would have been dark and edgy without falling into 'hypersexual serial killer trans' stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T08:08:10-07:00","id":1094133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094093#post1094093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll become a father this year. After a years of observation I'll have to be extra watchful to protect my child from world sickness. To be clear I'm not speaking about You or transgender persons cause they like everyone they could have good heart and be just a good people.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to protect your child from media, make sure to delay their going to 4chan and like sites until they can ignore the garbage signals on the internet and know what BS gets thrown around. That's probably much all the protection from media that you'll need to foster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nowdays I feel that beeing christian means to belong to marginalized and oppressed group. And I live in catholic country. Don't want to know how it looks in western Europe, but from my firneds told me. Bad. </div> </div> </div>If you're a Roman Catholic in Poland, you're almost certainly not oppressed, or at least, not because you're Roman Catholic. What it is that you're feeling is the crumbling of media exclusively catering to Roman Catholic mores. Not being catered to to the near-exclusion of everyone else is still oceans away from being oppressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T08:35:31-07:00","id":1094150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094118#post1094118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That you describe trans people as &amp;quot;girls with dicks&amp;quot;? Not okay. I'm hoping this is just a language and cultural issue. Please tell me it is.</div> </div> </div> </div> It just language nothing more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T08:38:58-07:00","id":1094154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094093#post1094093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowdays I feel that beeing christian means to belong to marginalized and oppressed group. And I live in catholic country. Don't want to know how it looks in western Europe, but from my firneds told me. Bad.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094133#post1094133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're a Roman Catholic in Poland, you're almost certainly not oppressed, or at least, not because you're Roman Catholic. What it is that you're feeling is the crumbling of media exclusively catering to Roman Catholic mores. Not being catered to to the near-exclusion of everyone else is still oceans away from being oppressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's some truth to both sides, so long as they're toned down. E.g. 'oppressed' is almost surely a too-strong word for the situation. <i>However</i>, it's true that in many European places, religious people (especially belonging to religions that <i>don't</i> have a reputation for being underdogs in the region and/or conservative and/or authoritarian ones) have become deemed as 'acceptable targets' lately, while other groups that used to be considered acceptable targets have become or are becoming unacceptable targets (e.g. various anti-conservative, countercultural, non-mainstream etc. groups).<br /> <br /> It's fascinating and scary how acceptable targets change as decades go by, but each decade the social consensus seems to think that it's totally justified in attacking their acceptable targets, while attacking non-acceptable ones . . . isn't. When I was a little kid, atheists were the consensus assumption and the religious were an acceptable targets; nowadays I'm looking Eastwards where atheists are an acceptable target and the religious are the protected class, and Westwards where in some places religious labels are used almost like a slur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T08:57:33-07:00","id":1094162,"title":"","content":"Poland changed. There are rift between generations of our grandfathers and nowday kids. Going to church makes you marked and uunpopular. I'm giving 20years for catholicism here. Second. There is a rift in the church cause last pope actions divided bishops. Most of them turned left and became more open . Many of them are pedophiles defended by church. Because of democracy there is group of protestants getting bigger each month calling openly catholics blind sheeps walking after false prophet. Second pagan cults are reborn but they are allowed to do their rites so they are happy in their communities. The only thing that people are afraid is islam. An in Warsaw there are some places where only muslims can buy homes. So it is a matter of years before we will have problems. I hope not but thats the reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T09:01:32-07:00","id":1094164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094118#post1094118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That you describe trans people as &quot;girls with dicks&quot;? Not okay. I'm hoping this is just a language and cultural issue. Please tell me it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I took no issue with it. I am a girl. I have a dick. I think it's important to be able to acknowledge that and discuss it openly, so as to help normalize it and dismantle the stigma against it. What I took issue with in Werewolf43's comment was the implication that media with trans characters is somehow inappropriate for children. That said, their kids, their choice, even if I disagree with that choice. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094125#post1094125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is also biologically incorrect. That would be more of an insult for intersex people who identify as female. A transwoman would be better described as transitioning or transitioned from men (male gender) to women (female gender), whether or not they have gone through sexual reassignment surgery. If they have experienced sexual reassignment, they no longer have male genitalia, so the insult would be inaccurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only &quot;biologically inaccurate&quot; if you assume gender is a factor of biology. I would be far more insulted to be called a man transitioning to a woman than to be called a woman with a dick. Especially because I'm not undergoing any surgical or hormonal transition, and have no plans to in the foreseeable future. To claim that calling me a woman with a dick is inaccurate is to invalidate my gender identity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094125#post1094125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with the representation of the trans person is that it made her sound like a sex-crazed serial killer, which is a stereotypical conservative representation of trans people from the 1990s. A more poignant and less stereotypical representation would have been a trans women who was Embraced before sexual reassignment and has to deal with a male sexed body that rejects the hormones she was taking to feminize her body and that heals any modification to her body, no matter how extreme.<br /> <br /> The horror would be the body horror of being eternally trapped in the wrong body, in a conservative undead society that rejects the claims that you are a woman, without any recourse except for insanity or suicide. Such a person would be tempted to join the Sabbat so she could benefit from Vicissitude in order to have the female body that she desires, but that may be just another form of insanity or suicide. That would have been dark and edgy without falling into 'hypersexual serial killer trans' stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree wholeheartedly. That said, a trans character who had not undergone sex reassignment before being embraced and was fully comfortable with that fact would also be perfectly acceptable representation. Better representation, in fact, as it presents the option of being trans without sex reassignment in a positive light, and avoids the common pitfall of LGBT characters always having tragic stories. And they could still be dark and edgy in the same way any cis character who doesn't struggle with gender dysphoria or body dysmorphia can be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-18-2017, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T09:32:26-07:00","id":1094181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094164#post1094164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, I took no issue with it. I am a girl. I have a dick. I think it's important to be able to acknowledge that and discuss it openly, so as to help normalize it and dismantle the stigma against it. What I took issue with in Werewolf43's comment was the implication that media with trans characters is somehow inappropriate for children. That said, their kids, their choice, even if I disagree with that choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, something about the comment felt pretty wrong to me. But as clarified, it's a language issue so all cool there. And yeah, the whole &quot;not for MY kids&quot; bit was also pretty teeth-grinding, but hey, I'm not going to ask if that's just some kind of language barrier and hope for the best. It is what it is, and nothing can really justify that to my eyes. But poor word choice can be forgiven.<br /> <br /> Gonna let that rest now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T09:39:00-07:00","id":1094184,"title":"","content":"Poor word choice, english at begginer level, especially times in language, shitty dictionary. Sometimes i cant find proper word like in ,,opressed&quot; case, learned by reading most from rpg like ways for l5r and wod suplements. Sometimes unawaring i'm just a jerk. Thats all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T11:18:53-07:00","id":1094231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094051#post1094051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My mom bought me Werewolf the Apocalypse at the age of 14 because I've been begging her to do so. I was amazed by Albrecht character in the comics - fallen garou hero - that was the main reason. Question is - would I buy WtA for my son/daughter if the main character would be a girl with d..k? No way. And I don't agree that WtA or Vampire is so mature. They want to make mature game, but in my opinion transsexual theme is no mature at all. It's just is.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm not going to do something silly like demand you go buy Exalted 3rd edition, but at least go look at the Exalted 3e promotional material and come back to this point after considering that there's a prominent trans character in Exalted 3e who is very much what most people looking for better representation are actually looking for instead of the idiocy that is Avery in the Prelude.<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> Also... can we please not get into the &quot;Christians are the new persecuted minority&quot; thing? Please? The last time it did not end well. There's a lot of people on this forum who belong to groups that face active threats of violence and death from Christian identifying groups on this forum. Nothing good comes of trying to compare that to the waning cultural influence of overt Christian values in Europe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094055#post1094055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But wanst Gore a important part of the aesthetic since the beginning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The early WW stuff didn't avoid gore all together, but the height of gore in the WoD aesthetic was really during the start of the &quot;playable antagonist&quot; phase of 2e. As well, I don't mind gore in my horror at all. But it's empty visuals without something with substance to justify it in the narrative. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094096#post1094096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if I missed the point on my last reply. Are you saying people would more accepting of new white wolf if they reached out more to people and explain their plans better?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe so. Everything I've heard is that the people that talk to them generally feel better about things. To me this means that they're capable of engaging with people in a fashion that convinces others they're good stewards of the WoD IP. By leaving lots of groups out of their engagement efforts, they're not making those pitches to those groups; making those groups more accepting.<br /> <br /> I spent the first year after Paradox bought the WW IPs from CCP trying to be positive. I spent a lot of time here trying to cool threads down, trying to give the WWP team the benefit of the doubt, trying to put things in contexts that were more charitable, and so on. I had a few encouraging emails with Tobias even. But they kept saying/doing things that they're blind to the reactions here, because they're not here. They're not addressing our concerns because they're not listening to them, because they're not engaging with us (and we've been told too many times to email/etc. them, they're job is to outreach to us).<br /> <br /> Like, the Ed Kramer thing. I get why they had no clue about that when they reissued the anthology to promote Martin's short story. I can forgive that. They weren't in the US gaming convention scene in the mid-90s to know what was going on before Kramer got caught. They weren't paying attention to the extremely minor impact Ed Kramer's arrest and conviction had in the news outside of the east coast US fantasy fiction and gaming communities. But they're <b>still</b> silent about it. No apologies to Ed Kramer's victims and families. No token corporate gestures like donating the proceeds (which can't be all that significant with Paradox's money backing them) to charities for the victims of predators like Kramer. Just... silence. If they were paying any attention to just these forums, they could have easily removed the Ed Kramer issue from the list of things people are holding against them. But they aren't listening, so they aren't fixing, so people continue to view them poorly.<br /> <br /> So it isn't just explaining their plans. It's also figuring out what people outside the LARP (and from what I've heard a narrower group of the overall LARP scene as well) care about. They need to hear when something one of them says comes off say, &quot;Fuck this part of our fanbase,&quot; instead of, &quot;Yay this other part of our fanbase.&quot; And they only way to do that is to be out in more places.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dasyrch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094056#post1094056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I see is that WWP as a Swedish company has a progressive/liberal culture that maybe can shock more conservative people from other cultures. I mean, is it ok to rip people while in Crinos but is not ok a trans character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it's not really shocking conservatives in other cultures. It's pissing off progressives and liberals in other cultures.<br /> <br /> Again, I can understand that a group of Swedes might not be aware of this, but the Avery character is a stereotype in the US that transwomen have been killed because of. Nobody has died because of a werewolf. People have died because other people spread the belief that transwomen a secretly sexual predators out to corrupt men and children. A person in the US seriously tried to use, &quot;I was so afraid when I found out she was a transwoman I had to kill her to protect myself,&quot; as a defense in court.<br /> <br /> Who do you think is shocked by the Avery character? Conservative bigots that think that transwomen can't be allowed in women's bathrooms out of fear of them committing sex crimes, or progressives that thought WWP was a progressive company but are putting out a transwomen character that kills men for voting for Trump as a validation of her gender identity?<br /> <br /> Also, it's not to say that US liberals and progressives don't deserve a good shock. The movie Get Out was fairly solidly aimed at white liberals that pat themselves on the back for not being racist while perpetuating racist systems, and it's a great movie for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems that wanting to speak about more 'real' stuff is annoying people, I read a review about the Mage Prelude saying that if they wanted to know about the refugee crisis they would have watched a documentary about that. It looks very narrow minded and that all the game is about is ripping enemies apart as some sort of superheroes-that-drink-blood or d&amp;d. </div> </div> </div>Rather, more specifically, speaking about 'real' stuff is annoying people when it's handled poorly. This is nothing new. WOD:G is considered one of the worst WoD books ever for good reasons. Charnel Houses is considered one of the best. They both deal with 'real' stuff very directly.<br /> <br /> I (keeping in mind I have not played because I will not buy, but I've read significant portions and reviews) see the issues with the Mage Prelude as not being, &quot;OMG, how dare they talk about the refugee crisis!&quot; but much more, &quot;Oh, good people/the Traditions are pro-refugee, bad people/the Technocracy are anti-refugee, complex real world multifaceted issue has been reduced to a simple narrative binary and ignores the complexity of the Mage factions in the process; this is lame.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T11:41:04-07:00","id":1094243,"title":"","content":"I've been skimming exalted v3. It is too big for now for me too read cause i have other book waiting so maby You could write more about that character. And I'm done about religion. But some threats from christian groups are ... Well shocking for me. Shitty situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T13:02:45-07:00","id":1094275,"title":"","content":"To the Avery argument: call me callous, ignorant, or whatever you want, but I just don't believe, on principle in exclusively positive representation, yes, even for marginalized groups. Sorry, but not sorry.<br /> <br /> I understand all the issues around it. I understand all the concerns all of you wrote about. I empathize with your situation, truly. I agree with the importance of positive representation for marginalized groups. It's just, there is a very, <i>very</i> fine line between &quot;not strengthening harmful stereotypes&quot; and &quot;positive discrimination in representation&quot; and I don't like the latter, because it's not good for any kind of art and ultimately it's just as much a lie as overly negative representation is. I won't go into a flamewar about it, I know a lot of you won't agree with it and that's fine.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this to defend the Avery character and the writing of the Prelude. Actually, I agree that it wasn't really good, it could and should be much better than that and it was just a wrong step to put her in that form into the first significant non-LARP product. However I won't laying all of that at the feet of Martin or any of them, since I don't know anything about how the approving process went and ultimately, neither of them wrote the piece.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm giving them slack for two reason still:<br /> <br /> 1. They have a small crew and doing a lot of things. I don't expect perfect handling and top-notch sensitivity, research and high-end nuance in all endeavors from them at this point. After a few years, when they're settled? That will be a much more serious question. They're seem spending most of their time organizing their big LARP events and developing V5 and i suspect a lot less energy went into the things that caused most of outrage.<br /> <br /> 2. There were a lot of things among what they said that I liked and the reports from the games and events they actually made/attended were overwhelmingly positive. Right now, that evens out the fuck ups, so I'm waiting for more info and ultimately for V5 before writing them off.<br /> <br /> However, I'm agreeing that they don't seem to spending much energy on communicating outside specific groups and events and that is error on their side. I'm willing to give them a slack still at this point, because the aforementioned lack of resources, but I <i>expect </i>it to change sooner than later, otherwise they'd just cut themselves off from a significant part of the fanbase and honestly, I don't think they're that stupid. Maybe they will launch their own forums, I don't know, but they need to do something.<br /> <br /> Also-also, going back to the topic of edgyness: I think what is considered &quot;edgyness for edgyness's sake&quot; and what is &quot;edgyness for a 'proper' reason/making a statement, etc.&quot; is highly personal.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not saying everything they did is great . They had some unnecessary fuck-ups and some statements I didn't like. It's just, at this point, I don't see the the sky falling, because their edgyness cut all the strings upholding it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-18-2017, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T13:50:50-07:00","id":1094290,"title":"","content":"It's entirely possible to responsibly portray characters of marginalized groups in a negative light. And I don't think the line is anywhere near as thin as you make it out to be. Look at Magneto. He's Jewish and a villain, without being a harmful stereotype of Jewish people or ridiculed for being Jewish. Boom, done, responsible negative representation.<br /> <br /> By all means, write trans serial killers, just don't make their MO tricking men into sexual encounters. Write vampires who are horrible people and also part of oppressed groups, not vampires who are horrible people <i>because</i> they are part of oppressed groups. The prince in my current vampire games is a trans man and an irredeemable bastard, but that's not problematic because his negative portrayal doesn't revolve around his gender.<br /> <br /> Re: edginess, I didn't say it had to be for a <i>proper</i> reason. It should just be for <i>a reason</i> other than &quot;cause it'd be shocking&quot;. Bring on the edge, but do so with intentionality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-18-2017, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T14:05:43-07:00","id":1094296,"title":"","content":"I think Heavy Arms makes some strong points, especially in regards to how LARP-heavy nWW seems.<br /> <br /> But I wanted to reply to Charlaquin's post in p.2, because it kinda rankled me a bit. <br /> <br /> I <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094088#post1094088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that she offers the driver sexual favors and then murders the driver if she didn't like his answers to her social justice questions presents her as both incredibly promiscuous and sexually predatory, both of which are negative stereotypes about trans women, committed to their views.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Promiscuous' and 'sexually predatory' are a common vampire trope, however. Why does positive representation have to supercede core themes of the genre?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094088#post1094088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that she claims her victims never refuse the offer of sexual favors is unrealistic, and suggests that either she is lying to make herself seem more sexually appealing than she is, or that she is using her vampire powers to take advantage of the men she is preying on. Neither option is positive trans representation, and the latter further doubles down on the stereotype of trans women as sexual predators.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I'd argue that either sounds plausible, and in the later case, using vampire powers to prey on their victims is the norm. Have we reached the point where the undead should be written to serve as positive role models? Because the character is transgendered, she should be treated as some sort of sacred cow?<br /> <br /> Look, I haven't read played/read We Eat Blood, and I'm not going to defend it's author's behavior, but on principle, why shouldn't this character recieve the same treatment as other monsters of the genre, if it's attempt is to portray vampires as such? A character should be written to be interesting, not to be either a positive or negative representation. Whether or not that was successfully done, I couldn't say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T14:27:53-07:00","id":1094307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094296#post1094296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Promiscuous' and 'sexually predatory' are a common vampire trope, however. Why does positive representation have to supercede core themes of the genre?<br /> <br /> Again, I'd argue that either sounds plausible, and in the later case, using vampire powers to prey on their victims is the norm. Have we reached the point where the undead should be written to serve as positive role models? Because the character is transgendered, she should be treated as some sort of sacred cow?</div> </div> </div> </div>See my post above. It is entirely possible to portray trans characters in a negative light, even in keeping with vampire's themes, without reinforcing harmful stereotypes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094296#post1094296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I haven't read played/read We Eat Blood, and I'm not going to defend it's author's behavior, but on principle, why shouldn't this character recieve the same treatment as other monsters of the genre, if it's attempt is to portray vampires as such?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because characters don't exist in a vacuum. <br /> &quot;Trans women are sexual predators out to trick straight cis men into sex&quot; is a real belief held by real people that actually gets people killed every day. As such, it is irresponsible to perpetuate that belief.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094296#post1094296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character should be written to be interesting, not to be either a positive or negative representation. Whether or not that was successfully done, I couldn't say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Writing characters to be interesting and writing characters responsibly are not mutually exclusive goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T14:38:05-07:00","id":1094310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094243#post1094243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been skimming exalted v3. It is too big for now for me too read cause i have other book waiting so maby You could write more about that character.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character in question is Prince Diamond. He's the cover character for the standard book, and the signature Eclipse. He's the most moral of the group - which isn't saying much - as he adheres to a very strict code of ethics based on his culture. This is also a culture that considers sword duels over the smallest insults perfectly normal behavior. So he's got a very strong sense of justice, but has been raised to enforce it with swift and brutal efficiency. He's also a sad character because he chose to take the guilt of one of his brothers on his own shoulders to be exiled from his people to save his brother, setting him on a quest to redeem the sins he's accepted by venturing out into the world and bringing justice with him.<br /> <br /> What's important about this? Where does his lack of a penis come in? Nowhere. Being a transman is an important part of the character (he'd very likely challenge you to a duel to the death if you called him a women), but his character isn't about being a token trans character (even if he was designed to make the Circle more diverse). He's a completely compelling flawed hero without being trans, and being trans adds depth and character to him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094275#post1094275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the Avery argument: call me callous, ignorant, or whatever you want, but I just don't believe, on principle in exclusively positive representation, yes, even for marginalized groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great. Nobody is asking for &quot;exclusively positive representation.&quot; People are asking for sensitivity regarding real world stereotypes. &quot;Mary Sue&quot; token minority characters are insulting too. But make a character that's flawed in compelling ways, not just playing on stereotypes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's just, there is a very, <i>very</i> fine line between &quot;not strengthening harmful stereotypes&quot; and &quot;positive discrimination in representation&quot; and I don't like the latter, because it's not good for any kind of art and ultimately it's just as much a lie as overly negative representation is. </div> </div> </div>No, there isn't. There's a giant clear line between the two.<br /> <br /> Where's the &quot;fine line&quot; between:<br /> <br /> &quot;Avram is a Ventrue banker that's notoriously greedy, stingy with helping other vampires, gleefully has a feeding restriction of only taking the blood of Christian babies, but you're supposed to think he's an awesome character because he uses his influence in the Jewish community to create conspiracies to attack the enemies of the Camarilla.&quot;<br /> <br /> And<br /> <br /> &quot;Baruch is a Ventrue banker who's lost his faith and replaced with with ruthless dedication to his own power and maintaining Camarilla control. Only able to feed on ritually impure Jews, he's used Dominate to get back at the religion that's failed him by bending a local Rabbi to his whims and to provide him his herd. He's needlessly abrasive to vampires that think of maintaining humanity as anything more than a practical matter, but every Neonate knows his money and influence in the financial sector is invaluable towards establishing a stable situation after they can no longer maintain any illusions that they're still alive.&quot;<br /> <br /> Neither of these are &quot;exclusively positive&quot; Jewish vampires. One's a mess of harmful stereotypes. One's a fully realized character who's faith while alive matters to his motivations, but is nastiness is because he's a vampire; you could adapt this to being a Christian/Christian trappings and it would change things, but it wouldn't feel improbable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. They have a small crew and doing a lot of things. I don't expect perfect handling and top-notch sensitivity, research and high-end nuance in all endeavors from them at this point. After a few years, when they're settled? That will be a much more serious question. They're seem spending most of their time organizing their big LARP events and developing V5 and i suspect a lot less energy went into the things that caused most of outrage. </div> </div> </div>They're a year and a half old, with an ever growing staff, and a lot of these mistakes are problems because they're not responding to people saying, &quot;Whoa guys, not cool.&quot; rather than them screwing up in the first place. Like I said. Them screwing up the Ed Kramer thing didn't surprise me. What bothers me is that they still have done jack shit about it.<br /> <br /> Forgiving some starting mistakes is easy... if there's an effort to correct them. If they continue to just sweep it under the rug and pretend it wasn't a thing, people will continue to be upset. 2, 3, 5 more year? Apologizing for promoting the work of a man that sexually abused children does not take years to do. It takes a well written blog post and hopefully some sign of contrition (again, something like donating the sales of the reissue to charities). A few days of work to correct a PR mess is well worth it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T14:53:17-07:00","id":1094312,"title":"","content":"Whats Baruch view on the Shoa? Even if he is only Ancilla he would have lost many members of his family there. Would you just ignore it? Because i would argue that that character can not be fully realized without even mentioning it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T15:16:48-07:00","id":1094317,"title":"","content":"There is a difference in being edgy and trying to incite a reaction. And that is where the new stuff is failing, more than anything else. For example, Avery (the trans vampire mentioned above) kills Trump supporters. Not 'politicians she doesn't like' or 'conservative assholes', just outright saying she kills those who voted for Trump. That to me is inciting a kneejerk reaction for the sake of it, without allowing the players to fill in the blanks. Also, boy does it date the game. With WtA, it is similar, Fenrir and Furies not caring about sjw or such things.<br /> <br /> With the WtA example, there is a worse aspect to it. If the Second Impegrium rumours are correct, Garou Nation has apparently decided that a wholesale culling of humanity's weakest is the way to go. This, at least to me, flies in the face of the themes of WtA and a lot of the tribes in the setting. First of all, the Impegrium happened during the very first cities of humanity, back when garou didn't even really have tribes or even the Litany. Second, garou are not vampires and live very short lives thanks to the war against the Wyrm. Most of the Nation are homid as well, grown up among other human children of their generation.<br /> <br /> Even if these kids embrace the life of their tribe and a more brutal culture, they still have learned about genocides and such at school. Not to mention the history of their own tribe. That is another thing that would stop a second Impegrium, the tribes have changed through the ages. Get of Fenris might respect strength, but their perception of what makes someone strong is more broad now. In addition, the tribe has had to deal with a faction that supported genocide of the 'wrong' kind of people, and that alone should make them think twice about Impegrium 2.0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T15:46:57-07:00","id":1094326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094317#post1094317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a difference in being edgy and trying to incite a reaction. And that is where the new stuff is failing, more than anything else. For example, Avery (the trans vampire mentioned above) kills Trump supporters. Not 'politicians she doesn't like' or 'conservative assholes', just outright saying she kills those who voted for Trump. That to me is inciting a kneejerk reaction for the sake of it, without allowing the players to fill in the blanks. Also, boy does it date the game. With WtA, it is similar, Fenrir and Furies not caring about sjw or such things.<br /> <br /> With the WtA example, there is a worse aspect to it. If the Second Impegrium rumours are correct, Garou Nation has apparently decided that a wholesale culling of humanity's weakest is the way to go. This, at least to me, flies in the face of the themes of WtA and a lot of the tribes in the setting. First of all, the Impegrium happened during the very first cities of humanity, back when garou didn't even really have tribes or even the Litany. Second, garou are not vampires and live very short lives thanks to the war against the Wyrm. Most of the Nation are homid as well, grown up among other human children of their generation.<br /> <br /> Even if these kids embrace the life of their tribe and a more brutal culture, they still have learned about genocides and such at school. Not to mention the history of their own tribe. That is another thing that would stop a second Impegrium, the tribes have changed through the ages. Get of Fenris might respect strength, but their perception of what makes someone strong is more broad now. In addition, the tribe has had to deal with a faction that supported genocide of the 'wrong' kind of people, and that alone should make them think twice about Impegrium 2.0.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah,that avery seems like a really badly written character. i can see why some people lost faith after that.<br /> About the second impergiun,i saw Shane Defreest (a WW employer) explaining the impergiun is something only aa small part of the garou want. He also said zak smith is not involved in any future projects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 05-18-2017, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T15:54:23-07:00","id":1094329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094326#post1094326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah,that avery seems like a really badly written character. i can see why some people lost faith after that.<br /> Abpit the second impergiun,i saw Shane Defreest (a WW employer) explaining the impergiun is something only aa small part of the garou want. He also said zak smith is not involved in any future projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, like, one poorly written character wouldn't ruin the company's image for me. But the fact that they failed to accept critique of the character, and in fact defended her, is a bad sign. And one more in a long series of PR misteps that they've failed to adequately address, and instead tried to defend. Apparently folks they've talked to have had their concerns alleviated, but I'm not seeing that in their public actions and I only have so much benefit of the doubt to give. I've gotten to the point now where I've lost hope for a V5 that would get me to give cWoD another try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T16:14:43-07:00","id":1094330,"title":"","content":"The Second Imperium is thematically a bad idea because the majority of WtA players in my experience want to play furry superheroes, not a fuzzy SS. In addition, Garou are outnumbered 1:500,000, so they have a vested reason to maintain the Veil. I would think that the Garou Nation would stomp hard on anyone who tried a Second Imperium to avoid the collapse of the Veil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T16:38:31-07:00","id":1094337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094330#post1094330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Second Imperium is thematically a bad idea because the majority of WtA players in my experience want to play furry superheroes, not a fuzzy SS. In addition, Garou are outnumbered 1:500,000, so they have a vested reason to maintain the Veil. I would think that the Garou Nation would stomp hard on anyone who tried a Second Imperium to avoid the collapse of the Veil.</div> </div> </div> </div>i don't think they're turning Apocalypse in a game about culling mankind. I think the second impergium is part of the metaplot,but that dosnt mean is something the player characters would have to participate in","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T16:44:48-07:00","id":1094340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094290#post1094290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's entirely possible to responsibly portray characters of marginalized groups in a negative light. And I don't think the line is anywhere near as thin as you make it out to be. Look at Magneto. He's Jewish and a villain, without being a harmful stereotype of Jewish people or ridiculed for being Jewish. Boom, done, responsible negative representation.<br /> <br /> By all means, write trans serial killers, just don't make their MO tricking men into sexual encounters. Write vampires who are horrible people and also part of oppressed groups, not vampires who are horrible people <i>because</i> they are part of oppressed groups. The prince in my current vampire games is a trans man and an irredeemable bastard, but that's not problematic because his negative portrayal doesn't revolve around his gender.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's where we won't agree. You're speaking about negative characters, whose existence as a member of a marginalized group isn't a significant part of them being a negative character, or just a tangential thing, or even a sympathetic aspect of an otherwise bad/controversial character, like in Magneto's case. On the other hand I <i>do </i>think that you could show characters, whose identification with a marginalized group plays a significant role in them being a bad character. Of course it could apply in reverse to positive characters too.<br /> <br /> Back to the Avery character (and I don't like the naming either, it's either thoughtless or intentionally jerky, neither is a good thing), whose &quot;MO is tricking men into sexual encounters&quot;. You know what? I talked about it with my homosexual and queer friends and we shared the opinion that it is, by all means not a representative character and even yes, a somewhat bad stereotype character, but it's also a plausible character. That a bitter person could use the power, gained by vampirism to take &quot;revenge&quot; on people who hurt and shunned her in her life, especially in a young vampire's case, when everything is still fresh.<br /> <br /> Was it fortunate to put it in a prominent role in a product which was, as I said, the first significant non-LARP product of the recent WW? NO, hell, it wasn't, especially in the recent political climate! I don't know how much free rein ZakS got in writing, but it was too much, IMO. Using a character like that isn't really problematic in my eyes, if there are other characters with healthy behaviours and personalities. So, the problem for me isn't the character itself, but the presentation and the context of the product.<br /> <br /> Reading <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar231_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"231\" data-vbnamecard=\"231\">Blitzburger</a> 's post and your answer to that, I think we just have a disagreement about the boundaries of representation in art forms. That's fine, I don't want to convince you, I think I understand why you have that opinion and I want to repeat, on a personal level, I'm sympathizing with it. I just also think, that in &quot;art&quot;, nothing is really off-limits (re: Charlie Hebdo...), but I also think that yes, writers/artist should be more considerate than ZakS was with this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094310#post1094310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great. Nobody is asking for &quot;exclusively positive representation.&quot; People are asking for sensitivity regarding real world stereotypes. &quot;Mary Sue&quot; token minority characters are insulting too. But make a character that's flawed in compelling ways, not just playing on stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although it sounds a bit like &quot;make a character which is flawed along lines I don't find insulting&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, there isn't. There's a giant clear line between the two. </div> </div> </div>Ok, I think both you and Charlaquin misunderstood me. It was my fault, I didn't pay full attention and English isn't my first language, so I'll try to do it better second time.<br /> <br /> The fine line isn't between non-stereotype character and a &quot;harmful stereotype&quot; one, but between not wanting to strengthen harmful stereotypes or treating those groups, as Blitzburger put it, sacred cows. Right now, it's awfully easy to slip into the situation, when any kind of negative picturing of a character from certain groups makes you an xyphobic/sexist/racist and people starting to light the torches immediately and I think it's equally harmful to picturing those groups in an overwhelmingly negative way, because both are skewed along an ideology. You just should show people as people, with the good and the ugly. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where's the &quot;fine line&quot; between: </div> </div> </div>See above. Otherwise, the example is interesting, so:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Avram is a Ventrue banker that's notoriously greedy, stingy with helping other vampires, gleefully has a feeding restriction of only taking the blood of Christian babies, but you're supposed to think he's an awesome character because he uses his influence in the Jewish community to create conspiracies to attack the enemies of the Camarilla.&quot;<br /> <br /> And<br /> <br /> &quot;Baruch is a Ventrue banker who's lost his faith and replaced with with ruthless dedication to his own power and maintaining Camarilla control. Only able to feed on ritually impure Jews, he's used Dominate to get back at the religion that's failed him by bending a local Rabbi to his whims and to provide him his herd. He's needlessly abrasive to vampires that think of maintaining humanity as anything more than a practical matter, but every Neonate knows his money and influence in the financial sector is invaluable towards establishing a stable situation after they can no longer maintain any illusions that they're still alive.&quot;<br /> <br /> Neither of these are &quot;exclusively positive&quot; Jewish vampires. One's a mess of harmful stereotypes. One's a fully realized character who's faith while alive matters to his motivations, but is nastiness is because he's a vampire; you could adapt this to being a Christian/Christian trappings and it would change things, but it wouldn't feel improbable. </div> </div> </div>No, the first is an intentionally bad writing of a Nazi-stereotype Jewish character, while in the second's case, that him was a Jew doesn't really matter aside from superficial things, he could be from any community, really. My opinion is that you <i>could </i>write a character, whose Jew identity is a big part of his personality, influencing his decisions, etc. It could be even stereotypical to some extent, because stereotypes are frequently rooted in reality, to some extent, that's (partly and not in every case) why they're stereotypes. It just needs to be convincing and needs really good writing, something Avery lacked. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're a year and a half old, </div> </div> </div>Not that long, in my eyes and they clearly had other priorities. Like, they organized several high-end events, but they still don't have a really &quot;proper website and messageboards? Yeah, i wrote it off as focusing on other things and lack of resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> with an ever growing staff, </div> </div> </div>Which is still very small (and for a considerable amount of time it was just Tobias and Martin) an Mr. Hite is, for example the first, who is really focused on the Tabletop side of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and a lot of these mistakes are problems because they're not responding to people saying, &quot;Whoa guys, not cool.&quot; rather than them screwing up in the first place. Like I said. Them screwing up the Ed Kramer thing didn't surprise me. What bothers me is that they still have done jack shit about it.<br /> <br /> Forgiving some starting mistakes is easy... if there's an effort to correct them. If they continue to just sweep it under the rug and pretend it wasn't a thing, people will continue to be upset. 2, 3, 5 more year? Apologizing for promoting the work of a man that sexually abused children does not take years to do. It takes a well written blog post and hopefully some sign of contrition (again, something like donating the sales of the reissue to charities). A few days of work to correct a PR mess is well worth it. </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, the following isn't apologizing for them, because I agree, they should step up their communication and soon. However, consider this (and I'll be intentionally blunt this time): on the big picture, we don't matter, not really. Most of the people commenting to their posts on FB, or on Twitter or people doing the same on other rpg sites are still don't even know about Onyx Path's work (sadly and I'm trying to mend it as frequently as I can). For a lot of the fans, WoD still ended in 2004. I had to explain to my roleplaying friends lengthily the existence of the 20ths <i>last year</i>! People are still asking &quot;wait there will be a new edition of Vampire?&quot;. Most of the people who consider themselves as fans or former fans, or would be fans of Vampire doesn't know anything about who Kramer is (I didn't know anything about him until it came up on these boards) or who ZakS is and what kind of conflict he had with other writers on various messageboards and in real life. And Frankly, they don't care about it either. Count the people frequenting these forums, the hard-core fans or the ones with some kind of personal investment, then count the ones really pissed by WW. We are a very-very tiny minority. The &quot;outrage&quot; about those controversial things most likely doesn't reach the threshold.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that WW shouldn't address those issues, because I think they should, but I have the self-crtitique to entertain the idea that it just isn't that important on the to-do list of Tobias, for example. Especially if they don't frequent these boards, although I agree, as soon as they have the manpower they should. But right now? I think reading forum posts isn't their priority. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T16:56:01-07:00","id":1094343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094312#post1094312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats Baruch view on the Shoa? Even if he is only Ancilla he would have lost many members of his family there. Would you just ignore it? Because i would argue that that character can not be fully realized without even mentioning it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um.... what the fuck?<br /> <br /> I hate to break it to you, but even Jews that lived through the Holocaust do not all define themselves by it. If you think you can't have a fully realized Jewish character without discussing their relation to the Shoah... I think you shouldn't be talking about what makes a reasonable Jewish character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T16:56:25-07:00","id":1094344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094326#post1094326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah,that avery seems like a really badly written character. i can see why some people lost faith after that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the first sting was what Martin said about NWoD. Then his opinion about incorporating real-world things, which is also a landmine for some people. Then came the hiring of ZakS and the Avery thing, which was the real slap, because a lot of upstanding members here and at rpg.net are friends of David A. Hill, or at least like his works and or/had personal bouts with ZakS. That was the deal-breaker in most of the eyes, I think, since if you're involved personally, you won't just shrug at something like that. I had really no horse in the whole thing, so it didn't affected me strongly. The Kramer thing went, in comparison, mostly unnoticed, IMO.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About the second impergiun,i saw Shane Defreest (a WW employer) explaining the impergiun is something only aa small part of the garou want. He also said zak smith is not involved in any future projects. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think too that people are getting into wild theories too soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T17:27:37-07:00","id":1094352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094340#post1094340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're speaking about negative characters, whose existence as a member of a marginalized group isn't a significant part of them being a negative character, or just a tangential thing, or even a sympathetic aspect of an otherwise bad/controversial character, like in Magneto's case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magneto's experience in a concentration camp is explicitly the reason why he can't accept the idea of humans and mutants living together in peace. Seeing the German people turn on their Jewish neighbors directly impacted is thinking regarding how to fight for mutant rights as a violent terrorist instead of Xavier's methods of political activism and doing good works.<br /> <br /> This is also a fictional mirror of real events where Jews that migrated to British Mandate Palestine from violent and even terrorist militias as tensions between the immigrant European Zionists and the local Arab Palestinians grew. Some of them, seeing what happened in the Holocaust, believed that the British and then the UN would not protect them and they'd be left to be crushed by the Arab countries around them, so they started attacking first.<br /> <br /> Saying being Jewish doesn't matter to Magneto's character is something you're going to have to back up a bit more than just dismissing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I talked about it with my homosexual and queer friends and we shared the opinion that it is, by all means not a representative character and even yes, a somewhat bad stereotype character, but it's also a plausible character. </div> </div> </div>How frequently are trans people in your country violently assaulted by people that have been lead to believe that trans people are actually a trap used by perverts to assault straight people?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That a bitter person could use the power, gained by vampirism to take &quot;revenge&quot; on people who hurt and shunned her in her life, especially in a young vampire's case, when everything is still fresh. </div> </div> </div>Except that's not the character we're talking about. She's been doing this for years. She's actively modified her hunting a few times as technology changed as well. She's not a fresh vampire drunk on power getting revenge. She's an experienced vampire that's killing people on flimsy pretense because she can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although it sounds a bit like &quot;make a character which is flawed along lines I don't find insulting&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Well, that's neither what I said, or the intention. As you recognize, stereotypes can be harmful. That's the key thing here, not my personal offense meter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You just should show people as people, with the good and the ugly. </div> </div> </div>OK... so what's the disagreement?<br /> <br /> Stereotypes are bad. Avery is a walking stereotype, not a showing of a person being a person with the good and the ugly. We want nuanced characters, even ones from minorities that aren't positive portrayals.<br /> <br /> I'm really not sure what you're trying to draw as a line now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, the first is an intentionally bad writing of a Nazi-stereotype Jewish character, while in the second's case, that him was a Jew doesn't really matter aside from superficial things, he could be from any community, really. </div> </div> </div>Most of those stereotypes predated the Nazis... but anyway, the thing about portraying people as people with the good and the ugly? People aren't that different. I'm saying this as a Jew: we don't come with some special unique thing that makes our story so unique that you can't tell an extremely similar story with a different ethnic or religious background.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is still very small (and for a considerable amount of time it was just Tobias and Martin) an Mr. Hite is, for example the first, who is really focused on the Tabletop side of things. </div> </div> </div>They're already bigger than Onyx Path is now, and have more financial backing to hire some community managers (which they need anyway if their plans for this year proceed as scheduled).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, consider this (and I'll be intentionally blunt this time): on the big picture, we don't matter, not really. </div> </div> </div>OK, this forum might not matter. But how many people here are parts of much bigger communities? How can WWP afford to write us off is they're not getting any input on a major part of their fanbase? We'll be eclipsed by the video games in due time of course, but gamers are sensitive to what grognards think. If all the TT fans come down on the new WtA video game as being not a real WtA game... it's going to hurt sales. There's lots and lots of video games, and people pay attention when the fans of an IP aren't on board with a game, because they can just skip that game and play something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of the people commenting to their posts on FB, or on Twitter or people doing the same on other rpg sites are still don't even know about Onyx Path's work (sadly and I'm trying to mend it as frequently as I can). </div> </div> </div>I find this a strange assertion. WWP's social media posts frequently promote Onyx Path projects. Even ones that don't involve WWP like Pugmire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying that WW shouldn't address those issues, because I think they should, but I have the self-crtitique to entertain the idea that it just isn't that important on the to-do list of Tobias, for example. Especially if they don't frequent these boards, although I agree, as soon as they have the manpower they should. But right now? I think reading forum posts isn't their priority. </div> </div> </div>And they're losing sales they don't have to lose for it. Worst, they're losing sales from people that would otherwise be out promoting the shit out of their products because we're hardcore fans.<br /> <br /> One one website I play, when C20's backer PDF dropped, I saw three people get ~two dozen others to convert within a few days. You can't ignore how important that is for a viable TT product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T18:04:43-07:00","id":1094369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094330#post1094330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Second Imperium is thematically a bad idea because the majority of WtA players in my experience want to play furry superheroes, not a fuzzy SS. In addition, Garou are outnumbered 1:500,000, so they have a vested reason to maintain the Veil. I would think that the Garou Nation would stomp hard on anyone who tried a Second Imperium to avoid the collapse of the Veil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was because all signs point to no Impergium being possible. There was an awful lot of fatalistic waxing poetic about it in the first Red Talons tribebook, or perhaps another place, where the viewpoint character starts talking about how there is a new Impergium - the one that humans practice against wolves - and there's not much that the Garou can do about it.<br /> <br /> In order to actually start an Impergium, thus, you need to be in a position of strength. That is not the position in which the Garou and Fera find themselves, save possibly the Ratkin, and they don't do things the way that the Garou do things.<br /> <br /> (footnote: I play Werewolf to play a ragemonster that can tear apart armored fighting vehicles, and who has the capacity to direct wrath toward targets that are possibly a bit more deserving of ultraviolence, like a much more up-front Devil Tiger who has already picked up the devil. For when you don't have the patience to be Willy Wonka all the time...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T18:07:28-07:00","id":1094370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094340#post1094340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's where we won't agree. You're speaking about negative characters, whose existence as a member of a marginalized group isn't a significant part of them being a negative character, or just a tangential thing, or even a sympathetic aspect of an otherwise bad/controversial character, like in Magneto's case. On the other hand I <i>do </i>think that you could show characters, whose identification with a marginalized group plays a significant role in them being a bad character. Of course it could apply in reverse to positive characters too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you <i>could</i>, but it's going to be much more difficult to do responsibly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094340#post1094340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the Avery character (and I don't like the naming either, it's either thoughtless or intentionally jerky, neither is a good thing), whose &quot;MO is tricking men into sexual encounters&quot;. You know what? I talked about it with my homosexual and queer friends and we shared the opinion that it is, by all means not a representative character and even yes, a somewhat bad stereotype character, but it's also a plausible character. That a bitter person could use the power, gained by vampirism to take &quot;revenge&quot; on people who hurt and shunned her in her life, especially in a young vampire's case, when everything is still fresh.</div> </div> </div> </div>She'd be a plausible character even if she wasn't trans. In fact, being trans makes her <i>less</i> plausible, because introducing herself as trans to random men, pointing out to them that she has a penis, and indiscriminately offering sexual favors to those men are all extremely out of character for the significant majority of trans women. I could still reasonably imagine such a person existing (in a world where vampires as presented in Masquerade exist, of course), but there's really nothing about her being trans that makes it any more plausible, and there is a lot about her being trans that makes it more harmful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094340#post1094340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it fortunate to put it in a prominent role in a product which was, as I said, the first significant non-LARP product of the recent WW? NO, hell, it wasn't, especially in the recent political climate! I don't know how much free rein ZakS got in writing, but it was too much, IMO. Using a character like that isn't really problematic in my eyes, if there are other characters with healthy behaviours and personalities. So, the problem for me isn't the character itself, but the presentation and the context of the product.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think Sarah Horrocks had more to do with the Avery character than Zak did. That was the impression I got from twitter, anyway. But, ultimately it doesn't really matter who is responsible, the character still perpetuates a lethally dangerous belief about trans people. As Heavy Arms mentioned earlier, transphobes aren't the ones being shocked by this portrayal. Many of them already view trans women as serial rapists who would kill their victims for having different political opinions if they could. This portrayal doesn't achieve anything except reaffirm those transphobes in their phobia. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094340#post1094340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar231_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"231\" data-vbnamecard=\"231\">Blitzburger</a> 's post and your answer to that, I think we just have a disagreement about the boundaries of representation in art forms. That's fine, I don't want to convince you, I think I understand why you have that opinion and I want to repeat, on a personal level, I'm sympathizing with it. I just also think, that in &quot;art&quot;, nothing is really off-limits (re: Charlie Hebdo...), but I also think that yes, writers/artist should be more considerate than ZakS was with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing is off-limits in art, but that doesn't exempt the artist from the consequences of their work. When you put a work of art into the world, you are responsible for the messages contained therein, and if that message reinforces harmful stereotypes of oppressed groups, you don't get to claim innocence when members of those groups call you out on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094340#post1094340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although it sounds a bit like &quot;make a character which is flawed along lines I don't find insulting&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could certainly sound that way to someone thinking along the lines of individual, rather than societal, impact. Ultimately, what I find insulting isn't important. What's important is what perpetuates harm against marginalized groups. So to rephrase slightly, &quot;make a character which is flawed along lines that don't make people feel justified in hurting me and others like me.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094340#post1094340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I think both you and Charlaquin misunderstood me. It was my fault, I didn't pay full attention and English isn't my first language, so I'll try to do it better second time.<br /> <br /> The fine line isn't between non-stereotype character and a &quot;harmful stereotype&quot; one, but between not wanting to strengthen harmful stereotypes or treating those groups, as Blitzburger put it, sacred cows.</div> </div> </div> </div>That line still isn't fine at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094340#post1094340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now, it's awfully easy to slip into the situation, when any kind of negative picturing of a character from certain groups makes you an xyphobic/sexist/racist and people starting to light the torches immediately and I think it's equally harmful to picturing those groups in an overwhelmingly negative way, because both are skewed along an ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really not. It's just that a lot of people are so worried that they'll be labeled as such for any negative portrayal that they refuse to accept any criticism on the basis of representation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094340#post1094340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just should show people as people, with the good and the ugly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but you should also consider the sociopolitical context your characters exist in when doing so, and take responsibility for the messages your art contributes to that sociopolitical environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-18-2017, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T20:19:32-07:00","id":1094400,"title":"","content":"And it is an implausible character. Transwomen are not instantly seductive. They have features that some straight men like, they have features that some gay men like, and so on. They will not magically fit every preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T20:23:05-07:00","id":1094402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094400#post1094400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it is an implausible character. Transwomen are not instantly seductive. They have features that some straight men like, they have features that some gay men like, and so on. They will not magically fit every preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair though, that particular aspect does get a little less implausible when you throw Presence into the mix. However, it gets a <i>lot</i> more problematic in the same stroke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T21:09:56-07:00","id":1094407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094402#post1094402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair though, that particular aspect does get a little less implausible when you throw Presence into the mix. However, it gets a <i>lot</i> more problematic in the same stroke.</div> </div> </div> </div>So wait, it is problematic for a trans character to be using basic Disciplines? Disciplines aren't employed so that vampires can act as meta-narrative moral exemplars; they are used so the undead can get blood meals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T21:11:49-07:00","id":1094408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094231#post1094231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe so. Everything I've heard is that the people that talk to them generally feel better about things. To me this means that they're capable of engaging with people in a fashion that convinces others they're good stewards of the WoD IP. By leaving lots of groups out of their engagement efforts, they're not making those pitches to those groups; making those groups more accepting.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had to boil down my issues with nWW into one single thing that all others descend from, it's this. They treat the TT fan base as non-existent, or of minor importance. Statements like &quot;the LARP community were the ones carrying the torch of the WoD after the end times books&quot; is pretty face-slapping. Just because they still had products coming out doesn't mean the demand for more VtM, WtA, etc had evaporated or that the people who played those games stopped supporting them. The response to V20 should have showed them that. The continued support for all the x20 products shows that. And it's because of that resurgence of popularity that nWW thought buying the WoD IP would be valuable. We tabletop gamers showed them it was definitely profitable.<br /> <br /> All the many faux paus they've made since the VtM5e announcement could have been smoothed over pretty well if they just explained their reasoning, gave some reassurances that those insensitive moments were honest mistakes, that they maybe worded things here or there poorly and they really meant this or that, or doing any of that. Instead, we're told to just email them. I mean, it's great that apparently they respond to some people's emails, but community engagement should be a big priority.<br /> <br /> The TT community might not be the biggest one but without it, Vampire: the Masquerade and the games that followed would never have been a brand worth buying in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T21:13:03-07:00","id":1094409,"title":"","content":"I think that the LARP community is a fairly small proportion of the cWoD players in my community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T21:18:04-07:00","id":1094410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094409#post1094409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the LARP community is a fairly small proportion of the cWoD players in my community.</div> </div> </div> </div>Larp players are the more visible though, I got into table top vampire after playing in a Larp setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T21:25:24-07:00","id":1094413,"title":"","content":"It depends on the community. I did not really associate with any LARP players until my 30s, and I had been gaming for 20 years before then in Charlotte, Norfolk, Research Triangle Park, and San Diego. Of course, when I did associate with the LARP players, I noticed that they tended to depend on one guy to buy all of the books, so I cannot imagine that the LARP players would be good customers, even if they are loyal to the brand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T21:40:51-07:00","id":1094415,"title":"","content":"At conventions would you be more likely to check out a room full of people dressed up and playing the same game or a group of people sitting at a table amongst a sea of people sitting at tables?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T21:44:08-07:00","id":1094416,"title":"","content":"So long as they continue to employ Zak S, V^2 will be too edgy for me even if it turns into a game of magical friendship where Malkavians spread joy and happiness in the form of Toki Wartooth-esque song numbers while Gangrel avenge Bambi's murder (which... I might actually play? I'm not sure, I've confused myself with this example.)<br /> <br /> I think that's an important distinction, to be honest. I can forgive attempts by a company that skew into 'too much edge' if they're made with good intent or out of ignorance. If, however, the <i>company</i> seems to be embracing a 'so edgy you guys' philosophy - and the handling of the whole Zak S debacle is exactly that in my eyes when coupled with a few other things like Martin's story and the Closet Incident - then I really can't be bothered. For a good example of this, Beast's initial version nearly did the same thing for me with OPP but a decently worded email from RichT and the attempt at making it not, you know, awful pushed the company back over the line because they were responsive without being dismissive, recognized an actual problem, and took steps to fix it. I don't think it worked, but one is good customer service and the other isn't. One shows that the company doesn't want to cause harm, the other suggests they are at best ambivalent towards doing so.<br /> <br /> If a game is a little too edgy, whatever. I can sand down the points until I'm happy with them, if I want to use it. If a company is too edgy or full of terrible people, though, I'm not going to give them my money regardless of the setting they put out. It's a rule I also apply to local businesses - if I know a store has knowingly employed someone who's done some horrible shit and isn't sorry for it, I'm going to spend my money elsewhere. And it's this more than 'oh no the setting edge!' that I think is where more of the lost profits are going to come from: boycotts over 'don't be awful', not 'how dare you talk about 9/11 or terrorism'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T21:44:54-07:00","id":1094417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094415#post1094415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At conventions would you be more likely to check out a room full of people dressed up and playing the same game or a group of people sitting at a table amongst a sea of people sitting at tables?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect the majority of tabletop gamers don't frequent conventions. I've never been to one myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T21:57:49-07:00","id":1094419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094417#post1094417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect the majority of tabletop gamers don't frequent conventions. I've never been to one myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are more table top games at gen con then live action ones, however the live action ones have better ticket sales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T22:13:05-07:00","id":1094424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094419#post1094419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are more table top games at gen con then live action ones, however the live action ones have better ticket sales.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really go to what I said, which is that the majority of tabletop gamers don't go to conventions in my opinion - which is, of course, <i>just</i> an opinion unless someone wants to dig up attendance data for a nebulous, broad, and ill-represented community. The proportion of tabletop games at one specific con vs live action games at one specific con only speaks to two things, which is the ease of running one and not the other in a limited timespan with players of unknown ability and sensibility, and perhaps the relative popularity of the two options among a subset of not even the gaming community, but specifically the gencon population pool - and even there, while many TTers have little to no interest in LARP, many LARPers have an interest in TT so it isn't as clearcut as 66% prefer TT to LARP.<br /> <br /> The reason I suspect most tabletop gamers do not frequent conventions is that conventions have three big challenges. Time, money, and accessibility. If you're working 9-to-5, 6 days a week? Most conventions are then either not an option or eating into unpaid or paid leave you might need for things like a family vacation. If you don't have the money to a, buy tickets, b, buy transportation, and c, buy accomodation (if you don't have friends in the area, etc, which for a lot of people is a reality when we're talking the big cons. Going to GenCon for me for instance would require me to rent a place as well as travel overseas etc etc), then you're up shit's creek without a paddle. Accessibility is the other, where there are people who either don't know the cons exist, don't want to go, or can't go because of travel restrictions, health problems, etcetera. As tabletop gaming is spread across more or less the entire face of the earth in one form or another these days, the pool of potential people who fall into this last category is huge, especially in combination with the first two. The dude making very little money in Swaziland can't come to Gencon even if he's spent more time running a dog-eared local translation of red box DnD he got from uncle than he has sleeping, but he is no less a part of the broader tabletop gaming community and population - though admittedly, he's probably representative of a very small part of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T22:19:16-07:00","id":1094426,"title":"","content":"Ok.............","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T23:27:51-07:00","id":1094440,"title":"","content":"Well. maby I'll just post excamples of things that are too edgy for me, it is more readable then my previous posts - rape, child abuse. Two thing I won't swallow, rest is more or less acceptable, cause it's well ... Words of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T01:02:02-07:00","id":1094450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094407#post1094407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So wait, it is problematic for a trans character to be using basic Disciplines? Disciplines aren't employed so that vampires can act as meta-narrative moral exemplars; they are used so the undead can get blood meals.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It's problematic to present a trans character that's supposed to be a kick ass positive portrayal as someone that uses Disciplines for the express purpose of getting unwilling men to engage with her in sexual situations to illicit answers to her &quot;purity tests&quot; which if you get right she they sexually assaults you for your being a good person, and if you get wrong she kills you.<br /> <br /> She doesn't need to mind-whammy men into sexual encounters to feed off of them. She does that because she gets off on it. And that includes doing it to the men she considers acceptable and are spared from her serial killing. Hell, if she's killing anywhere close to as frequently as she claims, she doesn't need to be feeding on the &quot;good&quot; guys at all. Which means it's even worse (assuming she's not just a liar), because she's frequently using Disciplines to remove men's ability to consent, just to give them a blowjob when she doesn't need the blood at all.<br /> <br /> There's no feeding/logical reason, at all, for her to have to sexually assault people via mind powers. Between guys that would just be down for a BJ and her sneaking in some blood via the Kiss to cover it up, and draining the men she kills, she'd be stocked with blood pretty much all the time. The only reasons that make any sort of sense is that she's a horrible person and is doing it for her own vanity (she can't take the rejection), or something like that.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> To the whole LARP vs TT and cons thing:<br /> <br /> It's so individual con dependent. I've been to cons were LARPs are the big thing and people barely TT. I've been to cons where TT is the big thing and there's one LARP that's poorly attended. I've been to ones where it's pretty even.<br /> <br /> The one con I've been doing yearly these days is very much a TT oriented one (though it's not a gamer specific con). This actually surprised the hell out of a few of us that tried to get LARPs going there the first few years because the general nature of the con and the crowd seemed way more LARP friendly. But the LARPs kept bombing, and the TT room was constantly full. So we stopped trying to make LARPs happen. It's a bunch of factors (how the con is run, who goes, what games people like etc.), but in the end, that's just how that con is.<br /> <br /> However, in my highly anecdotal experience, TT players are less likely to be con goers than LARP players. It's just the nature of the styles. LARPing is already more like a con for most people. It's less frequent, more players, bigger events, etc. Where TT is something you do at home with a few friends.<br /> <br /> One small con I used to go to was based out of a nearby college and was formed around their VtM LARP. The con was basically a big excuse to do a yearly major LARP event where alumni could come back and play their elder PCs to shake things up from the monthly normal LARPing of the undergrads playing the lower ranked vampires in the city.<br /> <br /> I've never seen a TT focused gaming group bother with that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T04:26:22-07:00","id":1094484,"title":"","content":"The majority of the cons that I have been to have had minor LARP participation. In my experience, LARP groups tend to be highly insular groups that make new people feel unwelcome through their inane internal politics and which alienate associated TT gaming groups (even the TT groups that help them get venues for $15 per weekend for the entire group of 40 people (yes, that comes from personal experience)). I have seen TT groups bend over backwards to help LARP groups, and I have seen them paid back with condescension from the LARP groups. The fact that WWP wants to prioritize LARP over TT sticks in my craw because I know that the majority of the sales and revenue come from TT players rather than from LARP players (meaning that TT players end up subsidizing LARP players).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T05:51:53-07:00","id":1094498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094416#post1094416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So long as they continue to employ Zak S, V^2 will be too edgy for me even if it turns into a game of magical friendship where Malkavians spread joy and happiness in the form of Toki Wartooth-esque song numbers while Gangrel avenge Bambi's murder (which... I might actually play? I'm not sure, I've confused myself with this example.)<br /> <br /> I think that's an important distinction, to be honest. I can forgive attempts by a company that skew into 'too much edge' if they're made with good intent or out of ignorance. If, however, the <i>company</i> seems to be embracing a 'so edgy you guys' philosophy - and the handling of the whole Zak S debacle is exactly that in my eyes when coupled with a few other things like Martin's story and the Closet Incident - then I really can't be bothered. For a good example of this, Beast's initial version nearly did the same thing for me with OPP but a decently worded email from RichT and the attempt at making it not, you know, awful pushed the company back over the line because they were responsive without being dismissive, recognized an actual problem, and took steps to fix it. I don't think it worked, but one is good customer service and the other isn't. One shows that the company doesn't want to cause harm, the other suggests they are at best ambivalent towards doing so.<br /> <br /> If a game is a little too edgy, whatever. I can sand down the points until I'm happy with them, if I want to use it. If a company is too edgy or full of terrible people, though, I'm not going to give them my money regardless of the setting they put out. It's a rule I also apply to local businesses - if I know a store has knowingly employed someone who's done some horrible shit and isn't sorry for it, I'm going to spend my money elsewhere. And it's this more than 'oh no the setting edge!' that I think is where more of the lost profits are going to come from: boycotts over 'don't be awful', not 'how dare you talk about 9/11 or terrorism'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand, I was sorely disappointed about them hiring zak . According to one employer he'll not be involved anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T06:10:59-07:00","id":1094504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094407#post1094407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wait, it is problematic for a trans character to be using basic Disciplines?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's problematic for a trans character to indiscriminately rape random men.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094407#post1094407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disciplines aren't employed so that vampires can act as meta-narrative moral exemplars; they are used so the undead can get blood meals.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in this case it's not being employed to get her blood meals. She could easily just eat her uber drivers without jacking them off first. She apparently uses Presence to get them to let her sexually assault them for... I don't know, she likes doing it, I guess? There inlies the problem. See Heavy Arms' post for a more in-depth answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T06:37:46-07:00","id":1094515,"title":"","content":"It's a little like, and god preserve me here because I just know this going to get quoted out of context at some point, creating an uneducated, smelly African-American character who goes around exclusively feeding off 'pure' 'virginal' white women with extreme violence, and doing so in the middle of an era of active lynchings like say the 1920s. In theory, none of those elements have to be racist - just like 'evil transwoman' and 'transwoman who is a sexual predator' aren't inherently transphobic or transmisogynistic concepts, because being black or trans doesn't preclude you from being violent or smelly or a rapist or whatever - but the broader cultural context makes it not only racist as shit, but outright irresponsible to go there. The same is true of 'transwoman who tricks/traps men into unwanted sexual contact then kills them', because that is almost literally one of the most pernicious<i> and current</i> stereotypes out there.<br /> <br /> We live in a world where 'trans panic' is a mitigating defence to <i>actual murder</i>. That's a true fact, and you can look it up, and almost universally where it's invoked it boils down to 'We were having sex/she was coming on to me/etc and then I found out she was trans so I flipped out and killed her'. It doesn't get people off the hook usually, but it does get them disgustingly light sentences for what boils down to 'I wasn't too careful where I put my dick so I beat someone to death'. That's without getting into the recent hubbub over bathroom rights and all the rest.<br /> <br /> Write trans characters. Write evil trans characters. But for fuck's sake, don't write characters that could pretty much word for word (just drop the vampire part in this case) be part of the actual rhetoric of hatespeech going around. That should be <i>obvious</i>. And saying it isn't, despite people's constant attempts to say otherwise in this thread and others, going for some kind of 'positive representation only!!1!!' benchmark. It's a basic benchmark of 'try not to write actual hate speech' - and I'm <i>reasonably sure</i> that we can all agree that as a benchmark, that's a pretty low damn bar to set!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094498#post1094498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand, I was sorely disappointed about them hiring zak . According to one employer he'll not be involved anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to hear, but I need to see it from an official source before I consider lifting my boycott.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T08:12:40-07:00","id":1094562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. <b>It's problematic to present a trans character that's supposed to be a kick ass positive portrayal</b> as someone that uses Disciplines for the express purpose of getting unwilling men to engage with her in sexual situations to illicit answers to her &quot;purity tests&quot; which if you get right she they sexually assaults you for your being a good person, and if you get wrong she kills you.<br /> <br /> She doesn't need to mind-whammy men into sexual encounters to feed off of them. She does that because she gets off on it. And that includes doing it to the men she considers acceptable and are spared from her serial killing. Hell, if she's killing anywhere close to as frequently as she claims, she doesn't need to be feeding on the &quot;good&quot; guys at all. Which means it's even worse (assuming she's not just a liar), because she's frequently using Disciplines to remove men's ability to consent, just to give them a blowjob when she doesn't need the blood at all.<br /> <br /> There's no feeding/logical reason, at all, for her to have to sexually assault people via mind powers. Between guys that would just be down for a BJ and her sneaking in some blood via the Kiss to cover it up, and draining the men she kills, she'd be stocked with blood pretty much all the time. The only reasons that make any sort of sense is that she's a horrible person and is doing it for her own vanity (she can't take the rejection), or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> You could make a functional Avery-like character being a trans sexual predator that hates men...if you were to make sure that she's a villanous character that doesn't represent trans people in general. Being a vampire isn't enough, being actually evil in fiction it's more than what you are or what you do.<br /> <br /> Writters have narrative tools to show an action as good or evil, that go beyond merely describing the action.. You can see this in fantasy and fiction very often:<br /> When a good paladin kills an orc, when the good US spy kills the bad nazi spy...the action it's deemed correct and somewhat validated by the world arround the character, the &quot;hero&quot; makes the kill and everyone it's happy.<br /> When a trully evil character does a kill, however, you're clear, thanks to the narrative, that his actions are reprehensible, you see how horrifying are his actions, you grow a hate on the character, you want the hero to appear and kill him.<br /> A Paladin can make a literal orc genoside look better than an evil wizard killing a single woman! And all of this is possible because the magic of narrative.<br /> <br /> If Avery was portrayed in a very negative light...making it crystal clear, with the power of narrative, that this is not how trans people act or should act, then it wouldn't be such a bad representation (if at all). There's words you should use to do this, and trans isn't the first one that should be used: Expressions like &quot;serial killer&quot;, &quot;rapist&quot; should come to describe her character earlier than &quot;trans&quot;, even if her motives are ultimately guided by her bad experiences as a trans person...<br /> <br /> Also, ideally, if you want your artwork to talk about sexuality, there should positive representation of trans too, otherwise it's incomplete (and ultimately wrong and damaging). A perfectly socialy acceptable ending of Avery arc would be to be killed by the Inquisition, at the hands of a trans hunter that was able to track her due her serial killer attitude.<br /> <br /> But nothing of this passed trough the minds of the people that were writting Avery's character. No, I'm sure she was supposed to be 'fun' in her edginess. I'm sure that what she does it's never trully questioned, because hey, she's a punk vampire and does what she wants...yeah! . I'm sure she was supposed to be cool because she's trans and kills pig man.<br /> We're not even exploring how her lack of humanity makes her a monster in comparisson with other trans people, let's the readers think about that to justify our work...meanwhile let's show her killing Trump supporters because that's totally what an inhuman monster should be doing and it's totally not a twisted attempt to appear as &quot;progressive people&quot;<br /> <br /> In other words, they tried to tackle a mature theme that's very sensitive issue and can cost the lives of people...and did a pretty lame work that's damaging to the people they represented. But instead of admiting that their work was far worse than Captain Planet trying to explain drugs to kids, they defend it and say that the people that attack their work can't accept seeing trans in media...now, that's an epic failure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Write trans characters. Write evil trans characters. But for fuck's sake, don't write characters that could pretty much word for word (just drop the vampire part in this case) be part of the actual rhetoric of hatespeech going around. That should be <i>obvious</i>. And saying it isn't, despite people's constant attempts to say otherwise in this thread and others, going for some kind of 'positive representation only!!1!!' benchmark. It's a basic benchmark of 'try not to write actual hate speech' - and I'm <i>reasonably sure</i> that we can all agree that as a benchmark, that's a pretty low damn bar to set!</div> </div> </div> </div>And yeah, this. Avery it's like saying the Syndicate it's a Jewish conspiracy that controls the world to beneffit Jews in detriment to everyone else's. What's shocking it's that the authors aren't doing this because they're facist conservative people that want to harm trans people 'cus they're unnatural. They did it to be progressist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-19-2017, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T08:42:22-07:00","id":1094571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094504#post1094504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's problematic for a trans character to indiscriminately rape random men.<br /> <br /> <br /> And in this case it's not being employed to get her blood meals. She could easily just eat her uber drivers without jacking them off first. She apparently uses Presence to get them to let her sexually assault them for... I don't know, she likes doing it, I guess? There inlies the problem. See Heavy Arms' post for a more in-depth answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow I missed that we were talking about Avery specifically; I thought we were just discussing trans characters using Presence in generalized terms. Yeah, I gotcha now.<br /> <br /> That being said, most of vampire is one big predatory rape metaphor; the crazy trans serial killer angle has been done to death (and needs to die), but it still seems weird to complain specifically about sexual assault in a game that features non-consent as a central (if quasi-metaphorical) pillar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 05-19-2017, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T11:48:51-07:00","id":1094628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094571#post1094571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Somehow I missed that we were talking about Avery specifically; I thought we were just discussing trans characters using Presence in generalized terms. Yeah, I gotcha now.<br /> <br /> That being said, most of vampire is one big predatory rape metaphor; the crazy trans serial killer angle has been done to death (and needs to die), but it still seems weird to complain specifically about sexual assault in a game that features non-consent as a central (if quasi-metaphorical) pillar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not complaining specifically about sexual assault, I'm complaining about a trans character being depicted as using her gender to trick men into unwanted sexual encounters. Again, characters don't exist in a vacuum, and this depiction is very close to a real-life stereotype of trans women that is regularly used to justify murdering us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T14:31:14-07:00","id":1094681,"title":"","content":"In most cases I see people were saying edgy in the sense of taking every piece to the extreme. Overusing and/or misusing the shocking value and adult subjects it\u2019s a very bad approach.<br /> <br /> So far, the new White Wolf has been making things like US comic book authors, dealing with mature subjects on their stories in an immature way, I don't read comic books, although, I read lists of &quot;mature/shocking&quot; moments made by comic book fans and they all were extreme resolutions of things that could be easily achieve by other means, but, sex and/or extreme violence had to be part of those moments. Side note, now some talked about X-Men, it\u2019s curious the \u201cgood\u201d mutants fight to keep the system and status quo by protecting those who reject them and they stop any attempt made by the \u201cbad\u201d mutants to change things for the mutants.<br /> <br /> VTM Prelude was edgy in a bad way, it has several moments of unnecessary sex, gore and scenes which tried to shock, but, in the end, they just feel silly and the reaction of the characters to those events doesn't help either and those happen one after the other, the gore is constant that it easily lost any impact. At least in that story, once a person is embraced it means they've already turned into a degenerated person from the very beginning:<br /> <br /> (SPOILERS) The ex was embraced by a Nosferatu? They\u2019ll have vampire sex just right after that, she only needed to ask. The same Nosferatu exhumed her dead husband to embrace him and failed in the process? No problem, at least she was able to reanimate his genitals somehow and that was enough and all she cared for. One character doesn't want to drink blood for several days? She's going to eat her own leg, instead, even if she\u2019s not a Nagaraja and that wouldn\u2019t stop her hunger for blood). Now, that's not a problem of those ideas offending me, they don't. Also, there\u2019s no average character or acts on this story, all of them went to the extremes.<br /> <br /> MTA Refuge was better (although, it doesn't make a good work in immersing you in the lore, all the characters have no time to explain anything), although, the sex scene was uncalled and forced, the classic moment when a film just adds sex scenes. On the other hand, they don\u2019t seem to know how to be subtle as they don\u2019t know how to give a reason and make it impactful to what the characters are doing, they were blatant with that blog post within the story and that\u2019s not going to be well received, if some people don\u2019t agree with their views, so a good intention and attempt to make things better it's going to fail.<br /> <br /> The introductory story in the revised edition is way better than any shocking thing that tried VTM Prelude, it has an interesting character that brings a lot of intensity to his narration, the recent story about the Baali in Lore of the Bloodlines is scary (psychological horror). Meanwhile, VTM Prelude has none of those things.<br /> <br /> In particular, I don't care about who's the author, my only concern about that was if that's affecting the promotion of WoD.<br /> <br /> I can understand those who are offended by the possible use of recent real life events from the world that happened close to them, but, at the same time, they don't seem to be concerned if somebody wants to write about other regions away from them, where human violence is constant and keeps happening since decades ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1846,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1846-nen","user":"NEN","date":". 05-19-2017, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1846-nen","name":"NEN","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T14:37:18-07:00","id":1094684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NEN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094681#post1094681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In most cases I see people were saying edgy in the sense of taking every piece to the extreme. Overusing and/or misusing the shocking value and adult subjects it\u2019s a very bad approach.<br /> <br /> So far, the new White Wolf has been making things like US comic book authors, dealing with mature subjects on their stories in an immature way, I don't read comic books, although, I read lists of &quot;mature/shocking&quot; moments made by comic book fans and they all were extreme resolutions of things that could be easily achieve by other means, but, sex and/or extreme violence had to be part of those moments. Side note, now some talked about X-Men, it\u2019s curious the \u201cgood\u201d mutants fight to keep the system and status quo by protecting those who reject them and they stop any attempt made by the \u201cbad\u201d mutants to change things for the mutants.<br /> <br /> VTM Prelude was edgy in a bad way, it has several moments of unnecessary sex, gore and scenes which tried to shock, but, in the end, they just feel silly and the reaction of the characters to those events doesn't help either and those happen one after the other, the gore is constant that it easily lost any impact. At least in that story, once a person is embraced it means they've already turned into a degenerated person from the very beginning:<br /> <br /> (SPOILERS) The ex was embraced by a Nosferatu? They\u2019ll have vampire sex just right after that, she only needed to ask. The same Nosferatu exhumed her dead husband to embrace him and failed in the process? No problem, at least she was able to reanimate his genitals somehow and that was enough and all she cared for. One character doesn't want to drink blood for several days? She's going to eat her own leg, instead, even if she\u2019s not a Nagaraja and that wouldn\u2019t stop her hunger for blood). Now, that's not a problem of those ideas offending me, they don't. Also, there\u2019s no average character or acts on this story, all of them went to the extremes.<br /> <br /> MTA Refuge was better (although, it doesn't make a good work in immersing you in the lore, all the characters have no time to explain anything), although, the sex scene was uncalled and forced, the classic moment when a film just adds sex scenes. On the other hand, they don\u2019t seem to know how to be subtle as they don\u2019t know how to give a reason and make it impactful to what the characters are doing, they were blatant with that blog post within the story and that\u2019s not going to be well received, if some people don\u2019t agree with their views, so a good intention and attempt to make things better it's going to fail.<br /> <br /> The introductory story in the revised edition is way better than any shocking thing that tried VTM Prelude, it has an interesting character that brings a lot of intensity to his narration, the recent story about the Baali in Lore of the Bloodlines is scary (psychological horror). Meanwhile, VTM Prelude has none of those things.<br /> <br /> In particular, I don't care about who's the author, my only concern about that was if that's affecting the promotion of WoD.<br /> <br /> I can understand those who are offended by the possible use of recent real life events from the world that happened close to them, but, at the same time, they don't seem to be concerned if somebody wants to write about other regions away from them, where human violence is constant and keeps happening since decades ago.<br /> <br /> In particular, I don't care about who's the author, my only concern about that was if that's affecting the promotion of WoD.<br /> <br /> I can understand those who are offended by the possible use of recent real life events from the world that happened close to them, but, at the same time, they don't seem to be concerned if somebody wants to write about other regions away from them, where human violence is constant and keeps happening since decades ago.</div> </div> </div> </div> god,that prelude seems worse and worse everytime someones tell me about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T15:51:24-07:00","id":1094709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NEN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094681#post1094681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, the new White Wolf has been making things like US <b>comic book authors</b>, dealing with mature subjects on their stories in an immature way, <b>I don't read comic books</b>, although, I read lists of &quot;mature/shocking&quot; moments made by comic book fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>You lost me.<br /> <br /> As a huge comic book reader, I couldn't disagree with you more. I'd say Image, DC, and hell...even Marvel have dealt with mature themes over the last two decades far better than anything White Wolf has done in a long time. Save for maybe Charnel Houses of Europe. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T17:14:47-07:00","id":1094725,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar95_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"95\" data-vbnamecard=\"95\">Fat Larry</a><br /> <br /> Well, better than WW is setting the bar too low, but I saw pretty bad stuff in Marvel and DC.<br /> <br /> Example: Wonder Woman in...Ukraine?...fighting the...russians?...and, when told that she was defending US interest, not those of the world, because of the FACT she wears US flag (please, don't say anything stupid to justify this, I know that Comics were supposed to be corny and patriotic back then, and anything you say to deny that she wears the american flag will just make it worse)...she does just what I told you not to do and tries to dismiss the issue saying something among these lines:<br /> &quot;ho, you think that this is the american flag just because it has stars and bars...many places have flags with those designs, it's just coincidence&quot;...and then she starts mentioning third world countries...<b>that either were or still are British...or US...colonies</b> (or have a similar relation).<br /> <br /> So, in one small speech the author manages to call readers ignorant for thinking Wonder Woman uses US flag (Why?. It was a 4th wall break, the excuse for an Amazon to wear US flag that readers are supposed to believe), demonstrates his own ignorance not knowing that isn't coincidence all of those countries wear similar flags but the consequence of a certain imperialistic agenda that has a lot to do with US, and shows brazen disregard for the way these countries were/are treated by US and/or Britain.<br /> Brilliant, not worse than the worst of White Wolf, but still remarcable.<br /> <br /> And on Marvel's side, there's things like Odin's father Bor's <b>unsolicited opinions about israel???</b> (that is a meme now) (Thor Girl has it's share of terrible writing...maybe not on WW level, but still bad)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now, let's not believe that I hate comic book or WoD writting. I like this game, and (usually) how it's written, and while I'm not a big comic book reader I've read pretty good stuff in comics. Generalization it's evil","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-19-2017, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T12:04:07-07:00","id":1095198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093986#post1093986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VV hasn't been released yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>VV will be released in Q1 of 2018.<br /> The (pre-alpha) playtest has been played on Saturday of the WoD Berlin event.<br /> It will be released to the public within the next one or two weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7336-teylen","name":"Teylen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T13:19:42-07:00","id":1095218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon