n imperialistic agenda that has a lot to do with US, and shows brazen disregard for the way these countries were/are treated by US and/or Britain.<br /> Brilliant, not worse than the worst of White Wolf, but still remarcable.<br /> <br /> And on Marvel's side, there's things like Odin's father Bor's <b>unsolicited opinions about israel???</b> (that is a meme now) (Thor Girl has it's share of terrible writing...maybe not on WW level, but still bad)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now, let's not believe that I hate comic book or WoD writting. I like this game, and (usually) how it's written, and while I'm not a big comic book reader I've read pretty good stuff in comics. Generalization it's evil</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay. Cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T14:12:30-07:00","id":1095239,"title":"","content":"In regards of the original question I don't think that they are being (to) edgy with VV.<br /> They do address various, current social and political challenges though, at least for me, those things I have seen, doesn't get across as exploitative or inappropriate. Though, maybe as a brief description from where I come from. I do follow White Wolf rather closely, attended the WoD Berlin event in regards of V5 Q&amp;A, Keynote, Playtest and the new Larp and am in general more tabletop oriented than in Larp.<br /> <br /> I do expect a contemporary tabletop RPG to address contemporary issues.<br /> Where in the past that's been things like the cold war and movements for environmentalism, currently its the more the challenges presented by terrorism, climate change and the like. They may address like the ongoing conflict in the middle east, the consequences of 9/11 and to a certain degree I do expect them to. I would as well expect that they do get people involved who were actually involved with the item at hand and can handle it respectfully.<br /> In general there weren't any statements that vampires would be all over 9/11 or that the middle-east would be portrayed in a fashion that be fit to make Homeland (TV series) blush.<br /> Rather quite the opposite. I do like how the New Cathars/Church of Caine feels a bit less like a club of evil fanatics, but something some christian vampires may develop as a system of believe.<br /> <br /> I did found some references to current German politics in regards of my character a bit challenging; I don't think I would create such a character myself.<br /> Yet I understood it not as being edgy or offer the edge, but rather as a task to portray that character, that I could accept or deny. Well or adapt to something more comfortable.<br /> <br /> In regards of the game, We eat Blood.<br /> Well I played it several times, to discover the various story elements, and do consider it well done. Otherwise it wouldn't have made sense to give it several runs.<br /> I don't consider the game transphobic, At the one hand because there are two characters in the game who are transwomen, which is a way higher representation than usual. At the other hand because while the description of Avery may come of as a bit crass, it is apparently inspired by a real life person. As the game doesn't make any reference to the use of Presence I figured that the character might just be exaggerating when claiming that every man is up for the toilet visit. Like normal people do when telling stories and wanting to impress on other people. Morally / humanity challenged vampires maybe lie even a bit more. My interpretation would, imho (d'uh ^^; ), fit the fact that Avery appears to be quite distressed when figuring that the main characters been piling up bodies like nothing good. Something that shouldn't worry her as much if she were such a serial killer.<br /> In general the character still read to me as good, but with a dark spot. Which fitted the narrative better than introducing a character that standsout by being good.<br /> The general tone. Well it, at least for me, hit a nice narrative tone that I would compare to the (early) Tank Girl comics or Transmetropolition. Which I both quite like, maybe even love a bit. While never getting so extreme as the comic The Filth, a comic that I might feel inclined to described as &quot;edgy&quot;/&quot;over the top&quot; edgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7336,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7336-teylen","user":"Teylen","date":". 05-22-2017, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7336-teylen","name":"Teylen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T18:14:06-07:00","id":1095309,"title":"","content":"First off, I apologize for my statements about Martin Ericsson in the last thread. I went too far and let my strong emotions get the better of me. <br /> <br /> But here's my two cents on the issue. I never liked personal horror or metaplot, which is why Revised Edition was never my cup of tea. If you like Revised, that's cool, but it's not for me. I unironically prefer katanas and heroism to personal horror any day of the week, but that is just my personal taste and nothing more.<br /> <br /> It looks like that V5 is going to be similar to Revised only in a more 2010's context rather than a 90's context. Combine that with the whole Zak S. debacle and other issues people have brought up concerning Mr. Ericsson and his vision for WoD, and I don't think V5 will be to my liking. As such, I will probably not buy it and just stick to playing my metaplot-free modified WoD using old books from 1e and 2e.<br /> <br /> I don't want to offend anyone with my post, I just wanted to explain that I don't have any interest in V5 and won't be supporting it. If you like personal horror, metaplot, and extremely dark and edgy fare, that's cool by me and it's your game anyway. I just don't want those things in my games and so as a Storyteller, I won't incorporate them. But again, that's just my personal tastes.<br /> <br /> So, personally I think V5 will be too edgy but that's only for me. Others may disagree. We'll find out when it is released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T22:40:10-07:00","id":1095370,"title":"","content":"The basic problem with a trans-driven narrative for a vampire premise is that the core identity crisis of the mortal frame is not only more or less irrelevant (immortal in a society of immortals with few if any sex-specific expectations nor any of the attendant biological baggage, to whom humans are pawns or cattle) but also pales so utterly in comparison to the new identity crisis introduced by becoming a bloodsucking, undying monster constantly locked in battle against murderous urges welling from deep within as to be laughably insignificant. It's not merely tasteless- it's outright a non sequitur that fits in extremely poorly with the overarching themes of the setting, even if it might be appropriate for a specific, highly idiosyncratic (read: not what you'd want in general teaser material for a setting) vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Comics are the last place I'd go for material that has dealt competently with mature themes, jesus christ. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 05-22-2017, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T23:00:10-07:00","id":1095377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1095309#post1095309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, I apologize for my statements about Martin Ericsson in the last thread. I went too far and let my strong emotions get the better of me.<br /> <br /> But here's my two cents on the issue. I never liked personal horror or metaplot, which is why Revised Edition was never my cup of tea. If you like Revised, that's cool, but it's not for me. I unironically prefer katanas and heroism to personal horror any day of the week, but that is just my personal taste and nothing more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered taking a Hakken character for a whirl? It may be a dramatically different context, but each one does carry around a katana... and a wakizashi. They're bushi Garou. And badly named for a group that's supposed to be ancient beyond humanity, but it's hopefully revised to be a Glass Walkers-type deal..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It looks like that V5 is going to be similar to Revised only in a more 2010's context rather than a 90's context. Combine that with the whole Zak S. debacle and other issues people have brought up concerning Mr. Ericsson and his vision for WoD, and I don't think V5 will be to my liking. As such, I will probably not buy it and just stick to playing my metaplot-free modified WoD using old books from 1e and 2e.<br /> <br /> I don't want to offend anyone with my post, I just wanted to explain that I don't have any interest in V5 and won't be supporting it. If you like personal horror, metaplot, and extremely dark and edgy fare, that's cool by me and it's your game anyway. I just don't want those things in my games and so as a Storyteller, I won't incorporate them. But again, that's just my personal tastes.<br /> <br /> So, personally I think V5 will be too edgy but that's only for me. Others may disagree. We'll find out when it is released. </div> </div> </div>What I disagree with you on is continually bringing up the metaplot and Revised. Werewolf in Revised was flying high and more or less free from Vampire, so it was kind of a case of &quot;personal horror? What personal horror?&quot; Especially when the metaplot for Werewolf, when it occurred, tended to have an extremely light touch. There was one exception to that in the form of the Ceilican getting stuff into the Spiral Labyrinth and coming out Hellcats, but for the most part, hooks were dangled so that player packs could be the center of the event and make a difference, as opposed to Vampire's patterns of &quot;you show up, watch elders you can't stop do something that you don't understand, and then go on to the next scene, where you watch elders you can;t stop...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T03:02:17-07:00","id":1095416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1095309#post1095309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But here's my two cents on the issue. I never liked personal horror or metaplot, which is why Revised Edition was never my cup of tea. If you like Revised, that's cool, but it's not for me. I unironically prefer katanas and heroism to personal horror any day of the week, but that is just my personal taste and nothing more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do understand your preference, yet I am not exactly sure if I get why second revised does disagree with you.<br /> Revise did, from my perspective, put the black shades on, unsheeted the Katana and jumped with it; for like fun.<br /> You could do the personal horror aspect or the metaplot - which went totally gonzo -, though there was a wide tone shift that did encourage a more heroic and over the top playstyle. Propelled by stuff like Underworld or Blade.<br /> <br /> VV won't have a Metaplot like revised, where signature character ran around and in the end did the cool stuff but is announced to focus more on the personal aspect of the signature characters enabling the player (characters) to do what matters and is cool.<br /> <br /> Sure, you can do all the political commentary or the personal horror stuff, include metaplot things about the middle east, but you are equally free to just outright ignore it.<br /> Then you'll have a new edition of a system and a game that does, at least in the playtest, in my opinion, flows a bit more smoothly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As such, I will probably not buy it and just stick to playing my metaplot-free modified WoD using old books from 1e and 2e. </div> </div> </div>They will structure the books with a:<br /> Core book that covers the rules and core aspects of the setting. A setting book for the Camarilla and the Anarchs each, which are planned to be all about the setting, probably got some Metaplot in them, and aren't supposed to have rules.<br /> <br /> It might be worth to give the core book a try, and maybe ignore the setting books, do them more to your own vision of VtM.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10809\" data-vbnamecard=\"10809\">Andkat</a> While I do agree that the core theme is in essence a coming of age story in regards of transformation, I do find it challenging that every notion of the previous gender does disappear and all vampires identify as gender neutral. I might consider an approach like this kinda inappropriate as it eradicates quite an important aspect of a human like creatures personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7336-teylen","name":"Teylen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T03:06:57-07:00","id":1095419,"title":"","content":"I don't really think it's fair to say Underworld influenced VtM Revised. <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20100608015709/http://www.avvo.com/case/view/collins-and-white-wolf-v--sony-pictures-11181\" target=\"_blank\">The other way around, on the other hand...</a> Personally, I've also always found 2E to be far more on the Katana and Shades side of the equation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T04:05:18-07:00","id":1095431,"title":"","content":"I didn't want to imply that Underworld influenced Revised, but express that it propelled a certain style of play that involved Katanas and Heroism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7336-teylen","name":"Teylen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T05:22:45-07:00","id":1095448,"title":"","content":"Underworld itself got released in 2003. It was pretty much the last year of the old WW releases, with a few exceptions, so...no, Underworld definitely did not influence Revised in any way.<br /> <br /> As for Katanas and Heroism playstyle..that didn't get influenced by Underworld either. As a matter of fact, the Katanas &amp; Trenchcoats trope comes well from the early to mid 90's.<br /> Heck, to me the one WW book that basically drips the stuff is..Mage, 1st Edition. Yep, first.<br /> Seriously, the artwork all over that book is katanas, blades and epic fights on rooftops. It's kind of amusing in retrospect.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> I mean, jeez. Look at the 1st edition storyteller screen: <a href=\"http://www.legrog.org/visuels/couvertures/1088.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.legrog.org/visuels/couvertures/1088.jpg</a><br /> It's like an overload of cringy awesome.<br /> <br /> I love that they actually used it as the interior panel cover for the M20 book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-22-2017, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T05:49:45-07:00","id":1095454,"title":"","content":"Well, memories can be blurry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Though luckily I did mention Blade as well.<br /> Which got released in 1998, thus close to revised. Plus it got Katanas, Sunglasses and even Trenchcoats, way more than Underworld <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7336-teylen","name":"Teylen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T07:47:24-07:00","id":1095474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10809\" data-vbnamecard=\"10809\">Andkat</a> While I do agree that the core theme is in essence a coming of age story in regards of transformation, I do find it challenging that every notion of the previous gender does disappear and all vampires identify as gender neutral. I might consider an approach like this kinda inappropriate as it eradicates quite an important aspect of a human like creatures personality.</span><br /> </span><br /> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> I'd argue simply that the psychiatric changes resulting from a near death experience into an actual transmutation into an undead man-eating monster probably introduce psychological perturbations larger in magnitude than the sum of whatever the person had previously, in addition to making many considerations irrelevant (e.g. any contribution to gender preference from sex drive is likely to be nullified by the loss of sex drive and replacement with a desire to stick your fangs into the jugular of anything that breathes). Basically, it is the largest possible disruption you could ever have in your life, such that the quirks of your psychology are both very likely to be knocked out of kilter by it and reframed in context of it; persistent identity dysphoria would likely reshape itself as something else (i.e. denial of the vampiric state) when plunged into outright vampirism. </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T23:04:39-07:00","id":1096991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094628#post1094628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not complaining specifically about sexual assault, I'm complaining about a trans character being depicted as using her gender to trick men into unwanted sexual encounters. Again, characters don't exist in a vacuum, and this depiction is very close to a real-life stereotype of trans women that is regularly used to justify murdering us.</div> </div> </div> </div>The WoD community is overwhelmingly progressive. I don't think the prologue writing reinforces anyone's stereotypes about trans people who's actually reading it, at least in a significant amount.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't do X in Y media because somebody might think it's real and act on it&quot; has been a pretty classical moral busybody defense for decades. Anyone who thinks that a transgender serial killer rapist vampire is an actual representation of trans people is an absolute moron. I recall similar whining about mortal kombat causing violence in schools, and my grandparents complaining about TV corrupting the youth before that. Media isn't real and claiming that it's getting people murdered or whatever other nonsense is just a lazy justification to censor stuff you don't like.<br /> <br /> I didn't think the Avery character was particularly interesting, if anything it looked more like a badly botched attempt by the writers trying to cash in on those sweet diversity dollars. I think it shouldn't exist because it's stupid, but I don't morally object to people writing garbage. <br /> <br /> Not sure how you can use the trans panic justification on someone who advertises that they are trans. Sort of incompatible. And I don't know about &quot;<i>regularly </i>used to justify murder.&quot; 19 trans people were killed or found dead from foul play in the U.S. in 2015. 15,696 people were murdered in the U.S. total in 2015. Estimates in the U.S. put 0.3% of the population as not identifying with their biological sex, which gives us 47 &quot;expected&quot; murders. USDJ says that approximately 52% of violent crimes go unreported, so we would expect 22 trans murders to actually be reported, which is a little <i>above</i> where the figure is actually at. Seems like trans people get murdered about as much as people who aren't trans. And trans/gay panic aren't, ya'know, legitimate defenses in court. Not for lack of trying, though. Trans panic has never been a successful court defense, and gay panic got charges dropped against 1 person in the 60s. Even the guy who got his conviction dropped from 1st to 2nd degree murder is serving 25-50 years. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11512-zanos","name":"Zanos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11512_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"550"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T23:04:39-07:00","id":1096992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1094628#post1094628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not complaining specifically about sexual assault, I'm complaining about a trans character being depicted as using her gender to trick men into unwanted sexual encounters. Again, characters don't exist in a vacuum, and this depiction is very close to a real-life stereotype of trans women that is regularly used to justify murdering us.</div> </div> </div> </div>The WoD community is overwhelmingly progressive. I don't think the prologue writing reinforces anyone's stereotypes about trans people who's actually reading it, at least in a significant amount.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't do X in Y media because somebody might think it's real and act on it&quot; has been a pretty classical moral busybody defense for decades. Anyone who thinks that a transgender serial killer rapist vampire advertising they're trans is an actual representation of trans people is an absolute moron. I recall similar whining about mortal kombat causing violence in schools, and my grandparents complaining about TV corrupting the youth before that. Media isn't real and claiming that it's getting people murdered or whatever other nonsense is just a lazy justification to censor stuff you don't like.<br /> <br /> I didn't think the Avery character was particularly interesting, if anything it looked more like a badly botched attempt by the writers trying to cash in on those sweet diversity dollars. Not to appeal to trans people, mind you, but to appeal to people who think that they're morally superior because they consume material that includes trans characters.<br /> <br /> Not sure how you can use the trans panic justification on someone who advertises that they are trans. Sort of incompatible. And I don't know about &quot;<i>regularly </i>used to justify murder.&quot; 19 trans people were killed or found dead from foul play in the U.S. in 2015. 15,696 people were murdered in the U.S. total in 2015. Estimates in the U.S. put 0.3% of the population as not identifying with their biological sex, which gives us 47 &quot;expected&quot; murders. USDJ says that approximately 52% of violent crimes go unreported, so we would expect 22 trans murders to actually be reported, which is a little <i>above</i> where the figure is actually at. Seems like trans people get murdered about as much as people who aren't trans. And trans/gay panic aren't, ya'know, legitimate defenses in court. Not for lack of trying, though. Trans panic has never been a successful court defense, and gay panic got charges dropped against 1 person in the 60s. Even the guy who got his conviction dropped from 1st to 2nd degree murder is serving 25-50 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11512-zanos","name":"Zanos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11512_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"550"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T02:03:57-07:00","id":1097045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zanos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1096992#post1096992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the prologue writing reinforces anyone's stereotypes about trans people who's actually reading it, at least in a significant amount.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't particularly recommend doing a lot of it... but have you read the Steam forums about it? 'Cause there's plenty of people on there (quibble as we want about how significant they are in actual number) that seem to test this assertion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;You can't do X in Y media because somebody might think it's real and act on it&quot; has been a pretty classical moral busybody defense for decades. </div> </div> </div>And overgeneralizations don't help anything.<br /> <br /> If you don't think irresponsible fiction can't contribute to real world violence, please explain the pizza-gate shooting. Yes, the Prelude is fiction. It isn't real. But that doesn't mean it is immune from irresponsible use of real world things; like stereotypes of oppressed minorities.<br /> <br /> Nobody is arguing that &quot;you can't do X in Y media,&quot; here. Some of us are arguing that Avery is an irresponsibly bad character uniquely to how she's written and talked about by the company that's responsible for the game/the writers of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyone who thinks that a transgender serial killer rapist vampire advertising they're trans is an actual representation of trans people is an absolute moron. </div> </div> </div>Right. To quote WWP:<br /> <br /> &quot;The criticized character, Avery, is perhaps the most helpful and kick-ass vampire in the game. She saves your ass and is (spoiler alert!) one of two main allies at the conclusion. Like Horrocks and Sabbath, we believe this character positively broadens the range of transgender portrayal in games.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the problem. WWP publicly states that they think Avery is an actual <b>positive</b> representation of trans people. That's... not good for our impressions of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't think the Avery character was particularly interesting, if anything it looked more like a badly botched attempt by the writers trying to cash in on those sweet diversity dollars. Not to appeal to trans people, mind you, but to appeal to people who think that they're morally superior because they consume material that includes trans characters. </div> </div> </div>Nah. I believe them when they say they're in it for the public perception of the company. That's sort of the root cause of the origin of this thread. The WWP team wants to push a very strong political stance, and keep pushing. Sure, there's a financial aspect to that. It's part of a brand identity that creates a fanbase and customers and such. But they've been pretty clear that they didn't just want people to feel good for purchasing material with diverse characters, they want to be seen as controversial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not sure how you can use the trans panic justification on someone who advertises that they are trans. </div> </div> </div>Um, nobody should be using trans panic as a justification for anything (besides pointing out how dumb trans panic is).<br /> <br /> But the character in question doesn't &quot;advertise.&quot; She waits until she has her target in a physical compromised situation to instigate her little purity tests and then reveals herself to push her testing farther. The issue is that trans people are persecuted on the grounds that they represent a hide danger. That some number of them are &quot;traps&quot; by people actually out to violate people using gender as a facade. That's the rationale behind bathroom bills: transgender people in bathrooms of their gender will allow sexual predators into bathrooms too. WWP is responsible for a piece of fiction that they claim is a positive representation of trans people... with a character that represents a vile trans panic stereotype. The fact that she's open about her gender identity to other vampires really doesn't change anything regarding how her feeding strategy is described.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I don't know about &quot;<i>regularly </i>used to justify murder.&quot; </div> </div> </div>How people justify persecution isn't the same as actual individual instances of it. How many trans people are murdered isn't the point. It's that trans panic is an ingrained social belief in a section of the population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T10:33:55-07:00","id":1097174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zanos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The WoD community is overwhelmingly progressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what?. If this wasn't the case, then the Avery character would have been either a ludicrously evil character...or nonexistent.<br /> <br /> And it seems that both would have been better scenarios as far as everyone it's concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T09:38:41-07:00","id":1097560,"title":"","content":"I just hope it's not as bad as Mage20 was. I have a pretty high tolerance for edginess, but having the book constantly go &quot;we don't want to offend anyone&quot; and &quot;we want to provide a safe space to game in&quot; while the book open with a piece of fiction involving <i>incesteous pedophilia</i> it's just tasteless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T11:15:45-07:00","id":1097571,"title":"","content":"I agree. Yes, that stuff occurs, but it is hardly relevant to the system. If it is a signature character, have the signature character do something cool rather than to show them being victimized. It is fine for backstory, but it makes horrible fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T13:04:38-07:00","id":1097600,"title":"","content":"Dunno, I liked M20.<br /> <br /> Phil Brucatto has a certain style, of course and I didn't like his every work (for example, his portrayal of the Hollowers in the Orphan's survival Guide, but generally I liked that book too), but I enjoyed M20.<br /> <br /> For the most part I don't like the whole safe space movement, for a lot of reasons, but I think gaming should be a safe space actually. Portrayal of controversial elements around the table should be consent-based. The WoD itself, however, I want it to be the very opposite of safe space and fiction is part of that, yes even fiction in the gaming books. I don't think every piece of fiction should be like that, but, when reading a WoD-related book, I'm fully prepared to seeing that moreso I'm somewhat expecting it, since, you know, it's the World of <i>Darkness... </i>It's a part of the package.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T13:34:47-07:00","id":1097608,"title":"","content":"I doubt anyone expects safe space from cWoD, but I do not want to read a fiction story about incestuous child rape, and I really do not think that there are many people who disagree with me on that on the forum. We are talking about books that parents share with their children because they want their children to get into gaming. That sort of fiction belongs in F.A.T.A.L., not cWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T13:53:01-07:00","id":1097616,"title":"","content":"Nah, it belongs in Black Dog Game Factory.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, there's still time to write Human Occopied Landfill in time with its 25th anniversary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T15:18:37-07:00","id":1097625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zanos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1096992#post1096992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The WoD community is overwhelmingly progressive. I don't think the prologue writing reinforces anyone's stereotypes about trans people who's actually reading it, at least in a significant amount.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't do X in Y media because somebody might think it's real and act on it&quot; has been a pretty classical moral busybody defense for decades. Anyone who thinks that a transgender serial killer rapist vampire advertising they're trans is an actual representation of trans people is an absolute moron. I recall similar whining about mortal kombat causing violence in schools, and my grandparents complaining about TV corrupting the youth before that. Media isn't real and claiming that it's getting people murdered or whatever other nonsense is just a lazy justification to censor stuff you don't like.<br /> <br /> I didn't think the Avery character was particularly interesting, if anything it looked more like a badly botched attempt by the writers trying to cash in on those sweet diversity dollars. Not to appeal to trans people, mind you, but to appeal to people who think that they're morally superior because they consume material that includes trans characters.<br /> <br /> Not sure how you can use the trans panic justification on someone who advertises that they are trans. Sort of incompatible. And I don't know about &quot;<i>regularly </i>used to justify murder.&quot; 19 trans people were killed or found dead from foul play in the U.S. in 2015. 15,696 people were murdered in the U.S. total in 2015. Estimates in the U.S. put 0.3% of the population as not identifying with their biological sex, which gives us 47 &quot;expected&quot; murders. USDJ says that approximately 52% of violent crimes go unreported, so we would expect 22 trans murders to actually be reported, which is a little <i>above</i> where the figure is actually at. Seems like trans people get murdered about as much as people who aren't trans. And trans/gay panic aren't, ya'know, legitimate defenses in court. Not for lack of trying, though. Trans panic has never been a successful court defense, and gay panic got charges dropped against 1 person in the 60s. Even the guy who got his conviction dropped from 1st to 2nd degree murder is serving 25-50 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a citation for trans panic never having been successful and the radically curtailed 'gay panic' statement? Because what you've just said literally flies in the face of a number of cases since the 1960s in various countries including America, and I'd like to see how you justify it. Please bear in mind that 'successful' does not necessarily mean 'charges disappeared!' - it means 'downgraded from murder to manslaughter', as that is essentially the entire point of the gay/trans panic defence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T16:05:10-07:00","id":1097630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097608#post1097608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt anyone expects safe space from cWoD,</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but I do not want to read a fiction story about incestuous child rape, and I really do not think that there are many people who disagree with me on that on the forum. </div> </div> </div>And I suspect the majority of WoD fans don't make a fuss over it. At all. Aside from that, it's tricky. I don't exactly <i>want</i> to read about horrible things, since they don't generate good feelings, but in certain contexts I don't have problems with them either. This is one of those contexts. Although, I acknowledge that everyone is different, with different sensibilities and expectations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We are talking about books that parents share with their children because they want their children to get into gaming. That sort of fiction belongs in F.A.T.A.L., not cWoD. </div> </div> </div>Really? I mean, <i>really? </i>You deem WoD as a good introductory rpg for new, young gamers and would share the WoD books with your children? Because I don't. I wouldn't give any WoD books to anyone who at least doesn't a teen and preferably a more mature one. It's just not a kid-game and it's not the goal of it and I don't want it to be the goal, there are plenty of games for that. I don't want a family friendly WoD.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T16:25:03-07:00","id":1097632,"title":"","content":"I started reading WtA when I was sixteen and I have friends that were introduced to cWoD when they were twelve years old. While there are aspects of cWoD that are too edgy for anyone under the age of 18, I have known gamers to introduce their pre-teen children to CtD and WtA as early as age 10. The simple game mechanics and the heroic character types of CtD and WtA make it very easy for pre-teens or teens to learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T16:27:40-07:00","id":1097633,"title":"","content":"Mechanics that are easy does not make the gamelines thematically appropriate in any sense for children. Sixteen is one thing - ten is quite another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T17:07:50-07:00","id":1097637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097633#post1097633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanics that are easy does not make the gamelines thematically appropriate in any sense for children. Sixteen is one thing - ten is quite another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.<br /> <br /> My opinion is still that WoD is not a game for children, despite the coolness factor and the light mechanics. Yes, you <i>could </i>make it lighter-tone, kid-friendly urban fantasy with badass characters having adventures in a modern setting and stuff, while leaving out all the more horrible details themes and tones, but it's not the default setting and I don't want the books to cater to that approach, there are other games for that. So no, I don't think the books should be something you could give to your kids to read.<br /> <br /> I was 16 or 17 too, when started with WoD and I had no problems handling it, it didn't give me nightmares or anything (although admittedly I focused more on the coolness aspect, than the personal horror aspect, and I'm still tending to lean a little bit to that direction I think), but still, I won't give the vampire revised books to my 10 year old niece, no way, not even if she would be interested in it and despite my high regard of the game and my love of it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-27-2017, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T18:19:56-07:00","id":1097647,"title":"","content":"I got into V:tM at around 10 and was running it and W:tA for friends by 12. We were fine. R rated movies weren't a mystery, and we all had library cards. That seemed to be enough psychological armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T18:46:37-07:00","id":1097658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097647#post1097647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got into V:tM at around 10 and was running it and W:tA for friends by 12. We were fine. R rated movies weren't a mystery, and we all had library cards. That seemed to be enough psychological armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Around 12-13, here, introduced with Vampire during the days of Kindred:the Embraced, but kicked it to curb for weresharks. After starting Shadowrun at about 10 or so, with its fake wink wink nudge nudge swearing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T20:49:42-07:00","id":1097677,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking there's a bit of a sliding scale here. Not every kid is going to be angling for the same material at the same time. There's no magic number on age where things suddenly start making sense.<br /> <br /> Also, there is a remarkable difference between the big 3 corebooks, and say, the Guide to the Sabbat or the Book of the Wyrm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T20:50:52-07:00","id":1097678,"title":"","content":"I think that there are plenty of people here who were exposed to cWoD when they were 14 years old or younger, so it is not unreasonable to expect that children will read the books. There really is no reason to have trans serial killers as iconic characters when all that it is going to do is prevent parents from wanting to get the books because they do not want their children to develop the wrong ideas about vulnerable populations. There is no reason to have child rape as the opening fiction when the majority of young players will find it so repulsive that they will just go play Pathfinder for the next decade instead of playing cWoD. I guess that I am trying to say that these type of things are not only tasteless, they are bad for business, and will end up dooming the gamelines by driving away the new customers that cWoD needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T21:13:27-07:00","id":1097683,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's fair to say that the intro fiction in Mage 20 was &quot;about&quot; incestuous child rape. There were two sentences in the entire story that reference a particular incident in a character's past, one line was fairly graphic (described as a sense memory of the survivor) and one much more vague . The story was about the two adult characters reconnecting, having been enemies and allies in the past. The fact that both characters were survivors of abuse was presented in a heavy-handed fashion, but was relevant as a point of commonality. And honestly, it's hardly the first time that rape, abuse, or murder has been portrayed in the fluff fiction of these source books.<br /> <br /> As a cis person, I don't feel like I have the right perspective to say whether or not Avery's portrayal was damaging. I don't however think that we need to shy away from complex and/or adult themes in general. These are games that, while played by children, have always been written toward an adult audience. And honestly, I would rather see World of Darkness make the attempt to include characters who are transgender or abuse survivors, even with the caveat that they're probably going to get them wrong sometimes. I'd rather see them learn to do better than not try at all.<br /> <br /> And I think it's fair to point out that we're talking about a nostalgia product from twenty-years ago, that got its resurgence through kickstarter funding and is solely distributed through a pdf/pod site. This isn't a matter of a thirteen year old finding a hardcover sourcebook in the local comic shop. The only people buying these books are adults. Odds are, the only children who ever encounter these books will be the children of the adults who already play this game. And that's the point when it's the responsibility of the parents to decide whether or not to present this material to their kids and if so, how.<br /> <br /> At the risk of being pretentious, I think that if White Wolf decides to create their new version of the World of Darkness to cater to those players who would see one admittedly graphic reference to abuse and go play Pathfinder instead, then it's definitely not going to be the World of Darkness that we remember and enjoyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 05-28-2017, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T21:19:10-07:00","id":1097684,"title":"","content":"Given that new White Wolf are the ones writing about full ass-rape stiffness, that seems unlikely to be the outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T23:45:24-07:00","id":1097701,"title":"","content":"I hear the new the new books are going to be so edgy they'll be gluing razor blades to the edges of the pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T00:04:49-07:00","id":1097705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097683#post1097683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's fair to say that the intro fiction in Mage 20 was &quot;about&quot; incestuous child rape. There were two sentences in the entire story that reference a particular incident in a character's past, one line was fairly graphic (described as a sense memory of the survivor) and one much more vague . The story was about the two adult characters reconnecting, having been enemies and allies in the past. The fact that both characters were survivors of abuse was presented in a heavy-handed fashion, but was relevant as a point of commonality. And honestly, it's hardly the first time that rape, abuse, or murder has been portrayed in the fluff fiction of these source books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how common that is in character backstories (not a good thing, mind), I hardly paid it any more attention than other awful things that the fiction presented. And if people wanna make the case of pedophilic rape in WoD? Clanbook Baali has that more than covered in its starting fiction.<br /> <br /> <br /> Back to the topic, though, it isn't that the things presented in the new things are in themselves awful. It is -how- they are presented that makes them so bad. Avery's badness is how her crimes and her tests are -all- tied to her being trans, or thing vaguedly relating to things most trans people agree with, like certain politics. It isn't done to showcase how messed up she is, either. It is rubbed in your face and the Trump part is so kneejerk it hurts.<br /> <br /> Or, this for WtA;<br /> <br /> <i>And in between all of that you have all of the other tribes who have their own ideas about how to deal with humanity and what we\u2019ve done wrong. The Black Furies are a matriarchal clan who don\u2019t want to help the humans until they sort out their gender rights, The Get of Fenris who just laugh at all of those social aims and say it\u2019s about survival of the fittest, and they should go into all-out war to see if humans can survive.</i><br /> <br /> Aside from the fact that garou are tied to humanity enough that there is no way Furies would ignore women in need, look at that Fenrir part. Those social aims sure sounds a lot like 'those sjws', and the war on humanity just adds to it. This is, again, in your face, asking you to react. Not presenting you a situation and asking you to think on it, as is more typical in WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 05-28-2017, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T01:57:24-07:00","id":1097716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097705#post1097705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how common that is in character backstories (not a good thing, mind),</div> </div> </div> </div>Do tell, how often is it?<br /> <br /> On topic: I look at it this way, Paizo wouldn't be anywhere near as big today if d&amp;d 4th Ed didn't tank as hard as it did. If 5th ed vampire tanks because it's the edgiest thing since the late night knife collection on qvc or it's system/plot is just exceptional some other company is going to produce it's own game line that's just similar but different enough to get a popular following.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 05-28-2017, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T07:24:54-07:00","id":1097764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097705#post1097705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from the fact that garou are tied to humanity enough that there is no way Furies would ignore women in need, look at that Fenrir part. <b><u>Those social aims sure sounds a lot like 'those sjws'</u>,</b> and the war on humanity just adds to it. This is, again, in your face, asking you to react. Not presenting you a situation and asking you to think on it, as is more typical in WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had no problem with what he said and I think that IS the perspective the many of the Get would have on numerous social issues, social media uses for it, etc. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T07:39:24-07:00","id":1097770,"title":"","content":"But that is not the WtA that I started playing when I was 16 and that is not the WtA that I want to support. There is nothing coming out of Paradox that makes me want to buy anything from them, and I am the type of gamer who is willing to spend $400-$800 on books every year. Now, I might be an exception, but I can afford to wait for Paradox to go bankrupt due to their bad business decisions (preferring LARP to tabletop, alienating loyal fans through 'edginess', pushing video games before using the tabletop games to build awareness, etc) and just get back into cWoD when a new company picks up the IP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T08:16:46-07:00","id":1097781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097764#post1097764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had no problem with what he said and I think that IS the perspective the many of the Get would have on numerous social issues, social media uses for it, etc.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have no doubt the Fenrir would think the matter as silly, but it is HOW it was said, again. It is very directly drawing reaction from the readers, as with all other WW5 content. Instead of being vague and leaving the moral grays there, they are egging the readers to react, not think. Like &quot;Oh, she kills Trump voters, I agree/Disagree with that!&quot;, or &quot;The Techies don't what refugees! That is good/bad!&quot;.<br /> <br /> It is not letting there be a space for the reader to look beyond the basic issue and the whole picture, instead it is drawing on on-the-spot reactions. That is my issue.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T09:14:21-07:00","id":1097796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097770#post1097770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (preferring LARP to tabletop, alienating loyal fans through 'edginess', pushing video games before using the tabletop games to build awareness, etc) and just get back into cWoD when a new company picks up the IP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a random thought: <br /> <br /> Sometimes, things get lost in translation. Especially when Martin, who's Swedish, is giving speeches in a dialect not his own. With that said, <br /> <br /> 1. Video games are where the money is. <br /> 2. Certain fans are going to feel &quot;alienated&quot; regardless of whatever the fuck white wolf does. Seriously. There is simply no possible way for 100% universal approval. Look elsewhere besides these forums, and you'll find plenty of people excited about the future of the WoD. For both LARP and TT. I for one, welcome the 'edginess'(god I hate that term).<br /> 3. You'll probably be waiting a while. Good luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T11:31:27-07:00","id":1097832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097701#post1097701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hear the new the new books are going to be so edgy they'll be gluing razor blades to the edges of the pages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I know where did you heard that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni",