y":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T13:17:04-07:00","id":1097857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097846#post1097846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wikileaks. It's in the dump that was released a few weeks ago, specifically the info taken from Godhand, the Vatican's elite espionage and hacking group. Apparently Godhand's been shadowing Martin Ericcson for years, both in the real world and online. Not sure why, but the files hint that there's a lot more to him than you might think. There was lots of obscure biblical stuff and old Latin and Hebrew I couldn't read, but a friend of mine who's studied those languages back in college said the passage claimed he's the 11th horn of the 7th head, whatever that means.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the leaked info wasn't complete, but it looks like something big is going down with White Wolf. And not just big, I mean big big. <i>Really</i> big. Edgy books, both literal and metaphoric are only the tip of the iceberg. Consider this a heads up. You've been warned.</div> </div> </div> </div>of course!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T14:51:42-07:00","id":1097874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097677#post1097677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking there's a bit of a sliding scale here. Not every kid is going to be angling for the same material at the same time. There's no magic number on age where things suddenly start making sense.<br /> <br /> Also, there is a remarkable difference between the big 3 corebooks, and say, the Guide to the Sabbat or the Book of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, of course. I watched adult horror movies in my early tens and most of the times they didn't give me the creep at all. I started reading Lovecraft very early and while I started playing VtM around 16, I actually read novels a lot earlier. I got an informative version of Dracula (a very shortened version, with a lot of pictures and educational content about the whole vampire myth and the original book and pop-culture connections. It is a quite good book, I still have it.) maybe even earlier than 10, I don't remember exactly when, and I was fascinated by vampires and overall the supernatural from that on. What I want to say is, yes there are children who could handle topics not even every grown-up could, but in general, WoD is not for children and I don't want it to be.<br /> <br /> I also agree with the remark that the big 3 cores are more mild than the supplements, although there are &quot;problematic&quot; things in the VtM revised core too, like the picture about ghouls slavering victims and lets not forget the whole theme of patricide in VtM. It's just not children material. I'd also argue that, while most of the &quot;edgier&quot; things were in supplements, those supplements are quite important ones, like a guide to one one of the main fractions of the game, or to the primary antagonist, or even the ST guide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097678#post1097678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that I am trying to say that these type of things are not only tasteless, they are bad for business, and will end up dooming the gamelines by driving away the new customers that cWoD needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tasteless is quite subjective, you'd hardly pressed to do mature content nobody at all finds tasteless and I'd bet it would end up a very sanitized and bland product. Besides, I don't think it drives away the kind of new customers it was aimed at, which aren't children and never were.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097683#post1097683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's fair to say that the intro fiction in Mage 20 was &quot;about&quot; incestuous child rape. There were two sentences in the entire story that reference a particular incident in a character's past, one line was fairly graphic (described as a sense memory of the survivor) and one much more vague . The story was about the two adult characters reconnecting, having been enemies and allies in the past. The fact that both characters were survivors of abuse was presented in a heavy-handed fashion, but was relevant as a point of commonality. And honestly, it's hardly the first time that rape, abuse, or murder has been portrayed in the fluff fiction of these source books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree. You know, I <i>love</i> people on the internet have the extraordinary ability to pick up one sentence, or picture and make a great fuss about it, like it was the core theme and biggest thing of that product...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a cis person, I don't feel like I have the right perspective to say whether or not Avery's portrayal was damaging. I don't however think that we need to shy away from complex and/or adult themes in general. These are games that, while played by children, have always been written toward an adult audience. And honestly, I would rather see World of Darkness make the attempt to include characters who are transgender or abuse survivors, even with the caveat that they're probably going to get them wrong sometimes. I'd rather see them learn to do better than not try at all. </div> </div> </div>Agree with that too. I don't want them to shy away from hard topics, or censuring themselves into one specific kind of portrayal. Yes, they'll misstep sometimes, that's a part of it too, but the sky won't fall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I think it's fair to point out that we're talking about a nostalgia product from twenty-years ago, that got its resurgence through kickstarter funding and is solely distributed through a pdf/pod site. This isn't a matter of a thirteen year old finding a hardcover sourcebook in the local comic shop. The only people buying these books are adults. Odds are, the only children who ever encounter these books will be the children of the adults who already play this game. And that's the point when it's the responsibility of the parents to decide whether or not to present this material to their kids and if so, how. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, thought about that too, I think you're right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the risk of being pretentious, I think that if White Wolf decides to create their new version of the World of Darkness to cater to those players who would see one admittedly graphic reference to abuse and go play Pathfinder instead, then it's definitely not going to be the World of Darkness that we remember and enjoyed. </div> </div> </div>Yup. Noticed the theme? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What I see is people have personal issues and trigger points they don't want to see in books (or strong expectations about how they want to see them) and differing levels of how much darkness they want to seep into the game from the real-world darkness of humanity. All those talk about &quot;edgelords&quot; and stuff is just the manifestation of that. That's okay, we aren't all the same, I can understand that. However, I think, as I said above, if you want to do a &quot;safe&quot; product, it'll be bland IMO and it won't be WoD at all. Thus they'll get push-back from some people and some outrage, but yeah, what I see outside this forum and rpg.net (and mostly from the same posters on both forums) is mostly a positive reaction toward WW. I'm not saying everything they do is perfect, absolutely not, they'd have serious missteps and V5 might be still a game I won't like in the end, but I don't hate them and actually what Martin said back about handling controversial topics, I fully agreed with that. I honestly think that it'll be too edgy to some people might be actually a good thing, ultimately.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097701#post1097701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hear the new the new books are going to be so edgy they'll be gluing razor blades to the edges of the pages.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Brilliant!<br /> <br /> Or they will just make the edges of the pages <i>very </i>thin. I see it will be a badge of honor to show off your scars from handling the book among your friends and every session will begin everyone cutting themselves with the attached razors and bloodying the pages...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-28-2017, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T14:52:16-07:00","id":1097875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097796#post1097796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Video games are where the money is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminded me I wanted to address the TT/LARP issue. I'm a TT player, I only dabbled in LARP and that wasn't even WoD, although I plan to try is sometimes. What I see is, yes, they certainly seem to have a bias toward LARP, although I'm not sure it is because their background or just a decision based on marketability. Yes, TT fans might buy more books worldwide, but WW said that they don't want to be an rpg publishing company solely, but a licensing and transmedia company and let's face it, LARP is just much more spectacular and better for brand recognition outside the hobby, especially the kind of high-end events they're doing (and also, the tickets are not exactly cheap). Although I feel they have a room for riding the current trend of TT streamlining and they might try, after the release of V5, I think. Still, a big crowd of people donning cool costumes and acting out their characters with passion and immersion, with the bacground of cool locales is just looks so much better on camera than several individuals sitting around the table. I'm not saying it's a better form of playing, as I said, I'm a TT guy, but I could see that LARP is just more media-friendly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Certain fans are going to feel &quot;alienated&quot; regardless of whatever the fuck white wolf does. Seriously. There is simply no possible way for 100% universal approval. Look elsewhere besides these forums, and you'll find plenty of people excited about the future of the WoD. For both LARP and TT. I for one, welcome the 'edginess'(god I hate that term). </div> </div> </div>I didn't like it either, particularly when it is used as a derision, but actually I started to come into terms with it, since it isn't a negative thing according to definitions and I don't give a crap about 4chan internet culture. Most of the great works were edgy for their times. I like edgy and I'm proud of it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-28-2017, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T19:40:01-07:00","id":1097939,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a cis person, I don't feel like I have the right perspective to say whether or not Avery's portrayal was damaging. I don't however think that we need to shy away from complex and/or adult themes in general.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree with that too. I don't want them to shy away from hard topics, or censuring themselves into one specific kind of portrayal. Yes, they'll misstep sometimes, that's a part of it too, but the sky won't fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that character is not tackling a &quot;hard topic&quot; any more than the Gypsy book tackled the rom. What it's doing it's offering an immature meme that any angsty teenager could have drawn, all while the authors praise themselves because of their dare.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with edginess, I think the M20 fiction was very decent and don't care a lot about the portrayal of child abuse. It was portrayed as the human horror the characters suffered in their childhoods, and thus as something to be fought. I agree in that these books aren't supposed to be for little kids.<br /> <br /> But, one thing it's to defend edginess (I can be on the same page about that, I like my gore and evilness in WoD), and other to stand at the side of utter bullshit. There's no reason to defend this kind of bad writting.<br /> <br /> God, Avery actually reminds me of some characters that my friends and I played with when I was 15. Up to the point of killing taxi drivers. :P Personaly, what I find surprissing (and depressing) it's not that the character it's &quot;bad&quot; (bad characters are legion in WoD), but rather that people defends it as a way to include lesbians in fiction. I tought that they were getting slightly more mature in revised...but well, these books ARE for angsty teenagers, not for adults, so I guess it was to be expected.<br /> <br /> What would have happened if WW said that Gipsy was an attempt to be edgy, and that the critics were just being racist?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-28-2017, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T21:22:57-07:00","id":1097975,"title":"","content":"Yes, I can just imagine them re-releasing an 'edgier' version of Gypsy, KotE, or KotEK that is filled with even more ethnic or racist stereotypes. They would then defend the characters by saying that people should be happy that they are portraying the character at all and that their 90s stereotype portrayal of each group is a 'positive' representation. The fact that they are going to get a 'Asian' to help write KotE, who could be anyone from a 4th generation British Indian to a 2nd generation German Kurd, fills me with dread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 05-29-2017, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T04:02:06-07:00","id":1098053,"title":"","content":"Will VV be too edgy? It depends on how much control Kenneth Hite is gonna have vs Ericson. Best case scenario they can give the later a Dracula doll to play in the corner while the adults are doing the work and he can feel validated somehow and doesnt interfere. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097796#post1097796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Video games are where the money is.</div> </div> </div> </div>If thats their aim then they are failing hard because as videogames the last 2 dont stand on their own. They made money because they pander to us, WoD/NWoD fans. They limited and clunky on the best of criticism. And at worse is a half assed product the likes i have never seen since M20 or duken nukem forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 05-29-2017, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T08:32:44-07:00","id":1098107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1098053#post1098053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>If thats their aim then they are failing hard</b> because as videogames the last 2 dont stand on their own. They made money because they pander to us, WoD/NWoD fans. They limited and clunky on the best of criticism. And at worse is a half assed product the likes i have never seen since M20 or duken nukem forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>lol. <br /> <br /> Do you know how long they've had the license?<br /> <br /> Do you understand how video game production works?<br /> <br /> The two &quot;games&quot; that were released on Steam WERE half-assed marketing products that were designed to keep up awareness on the universe. Some people liked it, some did not. Like myself. <br /> <br /> But to hold those two storytelling choose your own adventures against what the team at Cyanide is doing is ludicrous at best. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T09:47:58-07:00","id":1098125,"title":"","content":"There's a pretty big difference between one clearly misfired attempt at depicting a trans character and the mindset behind the production of the entire World of Darkness: G*psies book.<br /> <br /> This is NOT an attempt to defend Avery. But I think it's fair to highlight something <b>Aleph</b> said: that Avery is very similar to characters a lot of us created and played at age 15.<br /> <br /> Strictly in terms of &quot;edginess&quot;, it's hard to say she's anywhere near the level of past signature characters like Sascha Vykos. And I do think it's worth noting that a trans person was very involved in her creation. Obviously this doesn't negate the criticism of Avery's character. But I do think it shows the company's interest in representation rather than tokenism. Hopefully, they do end up incorporating the criticism, and Avery becomes the precursor to the inclusion of other, better developed and less harmful trans characters.<br /> <br /> Similarly, their idea of having an actual Asian person as lead developer of Kindred of the East isn't a bad one. I hope they choose someone who either has academic experience with multiple Asian cultures or they include Asian people from multiple Asian cultures on the development team. It doesn't mean that they will produce a good product, obviously. But I do think the emphasis on the points of view of actual Asian people for their Asia-themed product is a good sign that they're starting to learn from past mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T12:48:39-07:00","id":1098195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1097975#post1097975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I can just imagine them re-releasing an 'edgier' version of Gypsy, KotE, or KotEK that is filled with even more ethnic or racist stereotypes. They would then defend the characters by saying that people should be happy that they are portraying the character at all and that their 90s stereotype portrayal of each group is a 'positive' representation. The fact that they are going to get a 'Asian' to help write KotE, who could be anyone from a 4th generation British Indian to a 2nd generation German Kurd, fills me with dread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I highly doubt that's going to happen considering WWs stance on writing what you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T02:39:20-07:00","id":1098713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1093852#post1093852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When people say White Wolf is trying to be edgy, they often mean they trying to be shocking just for the sake of being shocking,Having gory imagery just for the sake of gorey imagery,having lots of swearing blood sex and gratuitious violence just for the sake of it. I've seen so many people worried about that and i don't know the basis of their concernsss</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I find all the swearing in the Mage rules to be annoying, rules should stick to being rules, not contests to see who can be the edgiest teen on the block.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T03:11:08-07:00","id":1098718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1098713#post1098713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I find all the swearing in the Mage rules to be annoying, rules should stick to being rules, not contests to see who can be the edgiest teen on the block.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which edition of mage are you referring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T22:52:41-07:00","id":1099029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1098718#post1098718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which edition of mage are you referring?</div> </div> </div> </div>They had an edition that didn't have swearing in the mechanics stuff?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I have a feeling of dread about the whole nWW thing. I started Vampire way back when when I was 13 (hey, I'm old, woulda been impossible to start out younger) and honestly, having had a pretty messed up childhood, none of it seemed particularly offensive or edgy. I look back, and sure I can see where people thought it but...eh. Fast forward and honestly...the world has gotten more jacked. We have an entire generation of kids that have grown up with things like terrorism, mass shootings, racism, sexism, whatever-ism as a pretty common thing.<br /> <br /> In this kind of world, trying to make an &quot;edgy&quot; RPG is pretty much going to require tasteless depictions of things to get any kind of reaction. And that doesn't contribute to a good story or gaming system. If that is the direction they take...eh...they are not really aiming for my money at that point, if I want tasteless random wannabe shock value stuff, there is all kinds of bs posted on the internet daily that is free that tries the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/690-fenris","name":"Fenris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T07:04:08-07:00","id":1099138,"title":"","content":"Terrorism has existed in the USA since the KKK was declared a terrorist organization by the federal government over a century ago, racism and sexism has always existed (and they are much less accepted than they were even 20 years ago), and mass shooting are down from 20 years ago. The problem is that cable news and the Internet increased the awareness (and occasionally glorify) such things beyond the local level. Of course, with global climate change, environmental degredation, growing inequality, and population growth, the world is looking more like cWoD every day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T08:45:46-07:00","id":1099163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1093829-is-vv-going-to-be-too-edgy?p=1099138#post1099138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terrorism has existed in the USA since the KKK was declared a terrorist organization by the federal government over a century ago, racism and sexism has always existed (and they are much less accepted than they were even 20 years ago), and mass shooting are down from 20 years ago. The problem is that cable news and the Internet increased the awareness (and occasionally glorify) such things beyond the local level. Of course, with global climate change, environmental degredation, growing inequality, and population growth, the world is looking more like cWoD every day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But that is my point, kids these days, even ones with 'normal' childhoods are exposed to far more of the crap going on in the world than most kids were when I was growing up. And its been that way for the past 16 or so years really, at least here in the US, European kids I can't really speak for, although I imagine due to globalization it isn't entirely dissimilar although the cultural connotations will be different. But the net result is that to get that shocked or &quot;omg that is jacked up&quot; reaction out of people takes more these days because we are so desensitized due to exposure. And if they are going to deliberately try to evoke that, and given what has been put out so far I have no reason to think they won't, I seriously doubt I am going to care for it. They could do a mature adult way of handling complex and dark subjects without going for the shock factor and really make it great, but considering the choices made so far, publicly, do you really think they will do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/690-fenris","name":"Fenris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T08:47:56-07:00","id":1099166,"title":"","content":"No, I agree, I think they will go for shock rather than handling it in a mature fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T12:16:10-07:00","id":1099233,"title":"","content":"Yeah it seems likely that they will go for the schlockiest version they can. Weaksauce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}